w","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/bb377151f470f9f4025c471f70f55c34dd6f0a7e","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKGJiMzc3MTUxZjQ3MGY5ZjQwMjVjNDcxZjcwZjU1YzM0ZGQ2ZjBhN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e","sha":"cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e"}],"sha":"bb377151f470f9f4025c471f70f55c34dd6f0a7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/bb377151f470f9f4025c471f70f55c34dd6f0a7e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:48:45Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T19:48:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): pass workflow_dispatch inputs to the shell through env, not templating (#450)\n\nAikido 232701801 (high, 75, template injection in GitHub workflow) on\nsandbox-deployment.yml: `${{ github.event.inputs.deployment-type }}` was\nexpanded into the run script before bash saw it, so a value containing shell\nsyntax would execute. The input is a `choice` (main/staging) today, which is\nwhy this was rated low-priority by the scanner and why it is hygiene rather\nthan a live hole — but the same pattern was repeated three times in\nproduction-deployment.yml, unflagged, and a future edit that relaxes the\ninput type would make all four exploitable at once.\n\nEvery input now reaches the script as an environment variable\n(DEPLOYMENT_TYPE_INPUT), and the later `git merge` lines read the shell\nvariable instead of templating env.DEPLOYMENT_TYPE back into the command.\nSame commands, same values; only the expansion point moves from the workflow\nrenderer to bash.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c6d07a195d15260761e636eed4fc17d7eecf6fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/0c6d07a195d15260761e636eed4fc17d7eecf6fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c6d07a195d15260761e636eed4fc17d7eecf6fe\nparent 55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1788896925 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788896925 -0600\n\nfix(ci): pass workflow_dispatch inputs to the shell through env, not templating (#450)\n\nAikido 232701801 (high, 75, template injection in GitHub workflow) on\nsandbox-deployment.yml: `${{ github.event.inputs.deployment-type }}` was\nexpanded into the run script before bash saw it, so a value containing shell\nsyntax would execute. The input is a `choice` (main/staging) today, which is\nwhy this was rated low-priority by the scanner and why it is hygiene rather\nthan a live hole — but the same pattern was repeated three times in\nproduction-deployment.yml, unflagged, and a future edit that relaxes the\ninput type would make all four exploitable at once.\n\nEvery input now reaches the script as an environment variable\n(DEPLOYMENT_TYPE_INPUT), and the later `git merge` lines read the shell\nvariable instead of templating env.DEPLOYMENT_TYPE back into the command.\nSame commands, same values; only the expansion point moves from the workflow\nrenderer to bash.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoGadCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmdgQAAIehOGOXsLZt6/EjEfXXtwg\nUxBoxYYEEzwlWfbtSgc0LwIxPqdm+xzOBiCrO1XUzkCQ4CscFT3urD+UPiyj52uH\n3mFkyK0pCDTnJjLoZhmuxCazIAtP888Hx7KA24b2Ydyy5KypcGXWGixzCEExCZNd\n2vCbkIclWa1DDqXJzkp7ZHGyW00Hsh1zuswUB8x3MD5K3W6/b2mDE2TwituZDH0C\njh1FD/+kz1vClro6bu9fDGt+pB2gOT0/hxbDXEkDWr4ACaFhaNKIPQWWeBepi496\nciVFwc+8TNOnNxK3xNAU+jfKIO8O17KYnELlvOjYdR11RVjekz9gqYuipejJiog0\nJVM69+vZRderzOH8dsgL7JkD7NHrwlb8BBaPf94u/Sx1HkVzMs7uVYbI00xDR8bf\nq2aGp0BjMJl5J4+K38i46hH8xyW+zvnFvQf2ruesyU+orll9VdmIZK34lB/z5xub\nj4teuq7AMnO+VQaihUxwybO9q3/dvPGNOzY/aSov5TLWLx0HDRBMcm6tjd/jMUZ4\nJu6Nn4rWKPrsuL2E4YlfTso7Bew265gjd8lu/rj1qkKZpa2l5mmzJhdikWsc/ubg\nVz+GM0IBsMv19l6dIIQYxsa7N8zbgsObXrdB2nvVN1ErW+VIWtAsNnWXXnSrmAHZ\nsd0CyUBkmg4Fh2KBOaI7\n=lUnT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T19:48:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKGNjMWNiNGFkMWZiOTVkMTk0M2QxZmE0NmJmZjRiMWMwMGVlYThiOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026","sha":"55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026"}],"sha":"cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/cc1cb4ad1fb95d1943d1fa46bff4b1c00eea8b9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:57:54Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:57:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): pin every GitHub Action to a commit SHA (#449)\n\nAikido 38638447/38638448/38638449/38638451/38638453 (high, 70): third-party\nactions referenced by a moving tag (localazy/upload@v1, localazy/download@v1,\npeter-evans/create-pull-request@v8, release-drafter/release-drafter@v7) and\none by a branch (Codium-ai/pr-agent@main). A tag or branch can be moved to\nnew code by the action''s maintainer or anyone who compromises that repo; the\nworkflows run with GITHUB_TOKEN, and localazy/release-drafter with repo secrets.\n\nEvery `uses:` now names the commit the tag pointed at on 2026-09-08, with the\ntag as a trailing comment so Dependabot and humans can still read it.\nactions/checkout@v7 is pinned the same way in every workflow for consistency\neven though Aikido does not flag first-party actions. No behaviour change:\nthese are the commits the tags resolved to today.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce2d219586df39e8b0e4dc4c39ae257ca5ed3cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/ce2d219586df39e8b0e4dc4c39ae257ca5ed3cf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026","verification":{"payload":"tree ce2d219586df39e8b0e4dc4c39ae257ca5ed3cf7\nparent c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1788893874 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788893874 -0600\n\nfix(ci): pin every GitHub Action to a commit SHA (#449)\n\nAikido 38638447/38638448/38638449/38638451/38638453 (high, 70): third-party\nactions referenced by a moving tag (localazy/upload@v1, localazy/download@v1,\npeter-evans/create-pull-request@v8, release-drafter/release-drafter@v7) and\none by a branch (Codium-ai/pr-agent@main). A tag or branch can be moved to\nnew code by the action''s maintainer or anyone who compromises that repo; the\nworkflows run with GITHUB_TOKEN, and localazy/release-drafter with repo secrets.\n\nEvery `uses:` now names the commit the tag pointed at on 2026-09-08, with the\ntag as a trailing comment so Dependabot and humans can still read it.\nactions/checkout@v7 is pinned the same way in every workflow for consistency\neven though Aikido does not flag first-party actions. No behaviour change:\nthese are the commits the tags resolved to today.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoFqyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlAsQAItAx27m8jXmBadKiX7JfMuT\nkbjAgt8c3Hj3Hjvih86kjJg/EzCkWwohKROuvOBX3V1me+NvsVWchozrBVOPs5dQ\nOzVoVXiXYxW2/6ldWPrHV7jq5zuPo3t1HrMGbH6dgxLcVo7ZqDuT/J/avKbcx9dn\nK+b9Y1mhm3rjwBuSvOrXWzR6X7dOWYAuKTnkSSmWPJ+pUPeogW1ARlteKDvQUx+t\n+JCgogZNy+rkh+Sv4LVJR6DpEcwOhOxel/r2CUrlwXUGAfqn/GtZKrfFpsqMeUVy\nBHdcB26in9k4gSMiqud4MXuzNKXQkXjdZiJkibeBGVNbjr8TXGGNvLVkOGIdfcCW\ntvHl0MA66kbk9gRns1P20DocgY2Bg8pdyB0Lx2Mud8nAwygqn/aKPdkNzsVGzzF1\n/73uNNJ7P4aDm3AdNDXcJ5wP7WSngDJGRtOF3Pjd8si0Knk7jfpSgNN+HVQhSt40\nwBkuOlnmxTU0yd/6p/oJwVsnOtMTrzK5Dls/bq5xo+tgQdp5GMfIeC1rPi5+f69q\n9RpFlhow/BjfjSODq+3ATfTUI/kpu2FE+i4FfjF1lHQdyKH+jESjdjW2+fU5oyXl\nJ40yHCduZFXgfrn2aT6HCG8A5lRLWWP+WywvN81ITbFtGPg75GMWfKYOzq2ZYh/R\nsRh2q3icGtnpcvLN2No9\n=sE6D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T18:57:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKDU1OTE4ZDYyNWYwMmY0NTk2NTc2NWI0MDhiYjZhYTY4YTkyMmEwMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de","sha":"c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de"}],"sha":"55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/55918d625f02f45965765b408bb6aa68a922a026"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:20:19Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T17:20:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(sast): only follow http(s) redirect URLs from the Redirect extension action (#448)\n\nAikido 159336707 (high, 75, AIK_js_xss_location): Redirect.tsx assigned the\nextension action''s redirectUrl field straight to window.location.href. That\nfield is configured by a care flow designer in Studio and reaches the patient''s\nbrowser as data, so a javascript: value would have run in the patient''s session.\n\ntoSafeRedirectUrl() now parses the value against the hosted-pages origin and\nreturns it only when the scheme is https: or http:; anything else yields null,\nthe activity is still completed so the care flow moves on, and a\nREDIRECT_URL_REFUSED warning is reported to Sentry with the activity id instead\nof navigating. Relative paths keep working (resolved against the origin).\n\nTests: 7 unit cases for the helper (accept https/http/relative, refuse\njavascript: in any casing, data:, vbscript:, blob:, file:, ftp:, mailto:, empty,\nnon-string, unparseable). tsc clean; full suite 43/43.\n\nThe remaining sink is a detector that fires on any non-literal assignment,\nverified by scanning the patched file with and without the suppression;\nsuppressed with a justified nosemgrep and recorded in the new register at\ndocs/standards/sast-finding-remediation.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"871e007ceda7709f6f8aeea61b92abef622519e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/871e007ceda7709f6f8aeea61b92abef622519e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de","verification":{"payload":"tree 871e007ceda7709f6f8aeea61b92abef622519e6\nparent 23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1788888019 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788888019 -0600\n\nfix(sast): only follow http(s) redirect URLs from the Redirect extension action (#448)\n\nAikido 159336707 (high, 75, AIK_js_xss_location): Redirect.tsx assigned the\nextension action''s redirectUrl field straight to window.location.href. That\nfield is configured by a care flow designer in Studio and reaches the patient''s\nbrowser as data, so a javascript: value would have run in the patient''s session.\n\ntoSafeRedirectUrl() now parses the value against the hosted-pages origin and\nreturns it only when the scheme is https: or http:; anything else yields null,\nthe activity is still completed so the care flow moves on, and a\nREDIRECT_URL_REFUSED warning is reported to Sentry with the activity id instead\nof navigating. Relative paths keep working (resolved against the origin).\n\nTests: 7 unit cases for the helper (accept https/http/relative, refuse\njavascript: in any casing, data:, vbscript:, blob:, file:, ftp:, mailto:, empty,\nnon-string, unparseable). tsc clean; full suite 43/43.\n\nThe remaining sink is a detector that fires on any non-literal assignment,\nverified by scanning the patched file with and without the suppression;\nsuppressed with a justified nosemgrep and recorded in the new register at\ndocs/standards/sast-finding-remediation.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoEPTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFWEQAHGAROSOQQrBzDvS1DIHeeoV\nwDBitj2DE0S5x+O7DCHc9T3prDlkZXsvDefGCQA0qX2eZKLoZawQMgfaxpqZWPfx\nTrXSq5gM3D8Zkd0gdeTy3G19uj20GkZZJHEcubD8CYDRyFAb9UjM8iJQ+Omi8KUn\nHIwo9wVCRq/pcsQVvtfXZ9d3NpN8/aH46Qqdi0poPvey0Rcga+49ICW+tFLeZkZt\nM+7lfPPTiEV+nxJr6xnjnSXDua1PfBtOqGyS0fs0yoh6L65OQFfT2WRdcgvduQ+q\n1GZKueVWXTmXXRRhCSQDG8AOlP3m4hZ9WgZ05iDcW4qK9GRW5KH/10+SXOs3T7HZ\nO91rFsWbW9iXJitLWoE66bFYk3jqQPyZX4GwcyX9gem5QackWrmY8dPAoCxdnTLU\nlUVmgGUCgaga6au3nq3q6+Ndj7xoxA0T7/5LxiW0D8MKGxfJcW9nggz27xLEtMiY\nwBN2sL6fPRvGB21EqsN97kUPdoZSu6W/ELYzyZjN+WmQIAKqrthDWZ0NMdPIoPgc\nWvd3nD1WBLszQMmMWvcEdJ4vcS4F7ATY+zbD5Vln5KE/7XHa9gJArqV0vlZoSzbA\nr2tnXFNM6t7DHH/4wF6T2k+KbaJ3dxJHLZYWgu/NGO0NQyuG9AllRdBBobLJgJCP\njh6+WWX0Y4DZRWoHO0gD\n=Wn2f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T17:20:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKGM2YTM0NjljNTU4OWRiZjAyYWIyZTY5NmVmYWQwNGIxNzk0MzE2ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226","sha":"23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226"}],"sha":"c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/c6a3469c5589dbf02ab2e696efad04b1794316de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44117299?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sharlotta93","id":44117299,"login":"sharlotta93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTE3Mjk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharlotta93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:12:35Z","email":"44117299+sharlotta93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abigaila Ekiert"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:12:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: pass pathway_id when evaluating form rules (#447)\n\n- Regenerate GraphQL types from the orchestration schema (codegen was\n  8 months stale), which adds pathway_id/activity_id to\n  EvaluateFormRulesInput.\n- useEvaluateFormRules now sends the current session''s pathway_id\n  alongside form_id/answers.\n- Widen the Form/DynamicForm cast passed to ui-library''s Traditional/\n  ConversationalForm to ''any'': the regen introduced\n  DataPointValueType.Attachment, which the pinned ui-library version\n  doesn''t know about, breaking the existing cast. Acceptable short\n  term since ui-lib is being migrated into this repo soon.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc8efb421dcb30de32cfab05d4f01bc159a1c701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/dc8efb421dcb30de32cfab05d4f01bc159a1c701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226","verification":{"payload":"tree dc8efb421dcb30de32cfab05d4f01bc159a1c701\nparent d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66\nauthor Abigaila Ekiert <44117299+sharlotta93@users.noreply.github.com> 1788455555 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788455555 +0100\n\nfeat: pass pathway_id when evaluating form rules (#447)\n\n- Regenerate GraphQL types from the orchestration schema (codegen was\n  8 months stale), which adds pathway_id/activity_id to\n  EvaluateFormRulesInput.\n- useEvaluateFormRules now sends the current session''s pathway_id\n  alongside form_id/answers.\n- Widen the Form/DynamicForm cast passed to ui-library''s Traditional/\n  ConversationalForm to ''any'': the regen introduced\n  DataPointValueType.Attachment, which the pinned ui-library version\n  doesn''t know about, breaking the existing cast. Acceptable short\n  term since ui-lib is being migrated into this repo soon.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATU