tml_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66","sha":"d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66"}],"sha":"23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/23d17b3c81d012f51614cd07f6db7b8b8bfbf226"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T14:37:10Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T14:37:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): re-resolve Next.js to 15.5.24 for the AVIF and Windows RCEs (#446)\n\nNext.js 15.5.23 is affected by two critical unauthenticated-RCE advisories,\nboth fixed in 15.5.24 (August 2026 security release):\n\n- GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4 (CVSS 9.5, Aikido AIKIDO-2026-553733, sev 95) — heap\n  buffer overflow in libheif when the image optimizer decodes an\n  attacker-controlled AVIF source. 15.5.24 disables AVIF optimization until\n  the upstream fix propagates.\n- CVE-2026-75604 / GHSA-p293-qw3h-jr36 (CVSS 9.0) — path traversal on a\n  Windows filesystem. Not reachable here; we deploy Linux.\n\nLockfile only: the declared range is already \"^15.5.21\", which spans the fix,\nso package.json is untouched.\n\nCarries sharp 0.34.5 -> 0.35.4 with it. Next 15.5.24 widens its sharp\noptionalDependency to \"^0.34.3 || ^0.35.3\"; 15.5.23 declared \"^0.34.3\" alone,\nwhich is what has been holding sharp below the patched 0.35.0 and keeping\nGHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj open. Not a separate change — it is what re-resolving\nNext now produces.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"52d03768f69dcd09bca7229ccf49d5826a4c831b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/52d03768f69dcd09bca7229ccf49d5826a4c831b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66","verification":{"payload":"tree 52d03768f69dcd09bca7229ccf49d5826a4c831b\nparent 6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1787927830 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787927830 -0600\n\nfix(security): re-resolve Next.js to 15.5.24 for the AVIF and Windows RCEs (#446)\n\nNext.js 15.5.23 is affected by two critical unauthenticated-RCE advisories,\nboth fixed in 15.5.24 (August 2026 security release):\n\n- GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4 (CVSS 9.5, Aikido AIKIDO-2026-553733, sev 95) — heap\n  buffer overflow in libheif when the image optimizer decodes an\n  attacker-controlled AVIF source. 15.5.24 disables AVIF optimization until\n  the upstream fix propagates.\n- CVE-2026-75604 / GHSA-p293-qw3h-jr36 (CVSS 9.0) — path traversal on a\n  Windows filesystem. Not reachable here; we deploy Linux.\n\nLockfile only: the declared range is already \"^15.5.21\", which spans the fix,\nso package.json is untouched.\n\nCarries sharp 0.34.5 -> 0.35.4 with it. Next 15.5.24 widens its sharp\noptionalDependency to \"^0.34.3 || ^0.35.3\"; 15.5.23 declared \"^0.34.3\" alone,\nwhich is what has been holding sharp below the patched 0.35.0 and keeping\nGHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj open. Not a separate change — it is what re-resolving\nNext now produces.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkZ0WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJUsQAGN+43mPAxPMUqFmgZUvIfRq\ne82gAjMYHV6watTh9wtrk61mht4RTy9Rsj3/oaK4gQi8YKHri6oR0aFzZvhjY+Sp\nl3dmbv2KdW/WIk2DR5SH7Xr/EC8h7EvyVh7J4uATv5DPoJanAcgwqu9KetnRIyWl\njshvRk/3XJyuo9FZzdTDCLTQpu+kGXZPUNDYK/WA4aStsgt0IOLNyb4ptiAsUz0a\n+PvJsB/4rSzsc4bmfOo66hsuC5T6fA6k2k/RTJCqHUgZTivzl6LxoMVtd8YWA938\nfJme166wvCGgl53Gva+QaWQls9QAFkGUlTjFMf1/KAcmNK58iBQjn0IQ9Uln5ZNc\n6MlORehJUTteBufBsNBdew6yQm0ZVGl+weDh3Uqgb8rqV8bcVeNYN+hRCLMlxzBP\nC+3Zbi2W7JdQx99sxe07Ndq5kSE+K9fC81XDrcuToBBl0pNQjG4eTeIFR3R0fPRV\nPryHv9ZchhTljgdtji2dlkEIHBIF7J8ErtCQtajpeVyXbbjSo0vXVcFV38sfTvW/\nhCzoWgBIR2KZW/6d1c1iDi/e/A+EGG2tuAaRCS6WfON1DzWytOT4kMTq8ZzSlKME\n2H37mFMyUM4bp7sMZF38i6UYazjNR3YMHskFUuDAh5twROc+mMhmTTP7+Yd/90xl\nH/MEDmdDVPpQ1JLprsg/\n=FmhV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T14:37:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKGQxMzkyODM2NTY2Njg5MGYxMDRkNTljZTJlNmFkZTllYjQ3ZDRmNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765","sha":"6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765"}],"sha":"d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/d13928365666890f104d59ce2e6ade9eb47d4f66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:56:21Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:56:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): upgrade Next.js to 15.x (#445)\n\nnext  14.2.35 -> 15.5.23\n\nClears ten high-severity advisories and two mediums:\n  CVE-2026-44578 (87), AIKIDO-2026-10758 (86), AIKIDO-2026-283297 (83),\n  AIKIDO-2026-573829 (83), AIKIDO-2026-284523 (82), CVE-2026-44573 (75),\n  GHSA-q4gf-8mx6-v5v3 (75), CVE-2026-64641 (75), AIKIDO-2026-10762 (75),\n  GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj (75), CVE-2026-64649 (65), CVE-2026-29057 (65)\n\nThis upgrade ALSO INTRODUCES one advisory, and that is not a surprise to be\nfound after merge:\n\n  sharp 0.34.5 is added to the tree (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj)\n\nNext 14 used squoosh for image optimisation; Next 15 uses sharp and declares it\nas an optionalDependency at `^0.34.3`. The advisory is patched in 0.35.0, which\nthat range cannot reach. The first Next release to relax it is 16.3.1\n(`sharp ^0.35.3`), so this clears when Next 16 lands, or sooner with an\noverride. Trading ten highs for one is worth it, but it should be a decision\nrather than an accident.\n\nWhy this is a smaller change than a framework major usually implies: the app is\nPages Router (there is no app/ directory), so the Next 15 changes that break\nmost upgrades -- async request APIs, RSC caching semantics, the client router\ncache -- do not apply. React 19 is not required either; Next 15 accepts\n`react ^18.2.0` and the app stays on 18.2.0.\n\nTwo config consequences:\n\n  - `swcMinify` is removed from next.config.js. Next 15 no longer recognises the\n    key and warns about it; SWC minification is the default, so the option was\n    dead weight.\n  - next-env.d.ts is regenerated by Next itself: it adds a routes.d.ts reference\n    and updates a docs URL.\n\nNot fixed here, and worth knowing: @sentry/nextjs now warns that\n`onRequestError` is missing from instrumentation.js. That hook is new in Next 15\nand the warning does not appear on main. It concerns errors from nested React\nServer Components, which a Pages Router app does not have, so the practical gap\nis small -- but adding `export const onRequestError = Sentry.captureRequestError`\nwould silence it and is a one-line Sentry config change, deliberately left out\nof a dependency upgrade.\n\nVerified:\n  yarn tsc --noEmit   clean, on TypeScript 4.7.4 (Next 15 does not require TS 5,\n                      unlike i18next 24 which is still blocked for that reason)\n  yarn test           36 tests across 5 files, all passing\n  yarn build          succeeds; 142 warnings, identical to main built with a\n                      cold .next cache; route set unchanged\n  yarn codegen        succeeds\n  smoke test          built app served on all locales -- correct lang attribute,\n                      correct i18n store, translated CTA in the server HTML\n                      (en/nl/fr/de/pl); browser load of /nl/preview hydrates with\n                      ZERO console errors and ZERO warnings, CTA renders as\n                      \"Probeer het uit\"\n\nBundle grows slightly: shared first-load JS 223 kB -> 226 kB, and the two\npatient-facing routes 453 kB -> 455 kB. Expected from the Next 15 runtime.\n\n@next/swc-win32-ia32-msvc leaves the tree (Next 15 dropped 32-bit Windows);\nirrelevant to the linux/amd64 deploy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f45207f1e392874c9d0723339394d1906bd56fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/1f45207f1e392874c9d0723339394d1906bd56fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f45207f1e392874c9d0723339394d1906bd56fa\nparent 632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1787259381 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787259381 -0600\n\nfix(security): upgrade Next.js to 15.x (#445)\n\nnext  14.2.35 -> 15.5.23\n\nClears ten high-severity advisories and two mediums:\n  CVE-2026-44578 (87), AIKIDO-2026-10758 (86), AIKIDO-2026-283297 (83),\n  AIKIDO-2026-573829 (83), AIKIDO-2026-284523 (82), CVE-2026-44573 (75),\n  GHSA-q4gf-8mx6-v5v3 (75), CVE-2026-64641 (75), AIKIDO-2026-10762 (75),\n  GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj (75), CVE-2026-64649 (65), CVE-2026-29057 (65)\n\nThis upgrade ALSO INTRODUCES one advisory, and that is not a surprise to be\nfound after merge:\n\n  sharp 0.34.5 is added to the tree (GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj)\n\nNext 14 used squoosh for image optimisation; Next 15 uses sharp and declares it\nas an optionalDependency at `^0.34.3`. The advisory is patched in 0.35.0, which\nthat range cannot reach. The first Next release to relax it is 16.3.1\n(`sharp ^0.35.3`), so this clears when Next 16 lands, or sooner with an\noverride. Trading ten highs for one is worth it, but it should be a decision\nrather than an accident.\n\nWhy this is a smaller change than a framework major usually implies: the app is\nPages Router (there is no app/ directory), so the Next 15 changes that break\nmost upgrades -- async request APIs, RSC caching semantics, the client router\ncache -- do not apply. React 19 is not required either; Next 15 accepts\n`react ^18.2.0` and the app stays on 18.2.0.\n\nTwo config consequences:\n\n  - `swcMinify` is removed from next.config.js. Next 15 no longer recognises the\n    key and warns about it; SWC minification is the default, so the option was\n    dead weight.\n  - next-env.d.ts is regenerated by Next itself: it adds a routes.d.ts reference\n    and updates a docs URL.\n\nNot fixed here, and worth knowing: @sentry/nextjs now warns that\n`onRequestError` is missing from instrumentation.js. That hook is new in Next 15\nand the warning does not appear on main. It concerns errors from nested React\nServer Components, which a Pages Router app does not have, so the practical gap\nis small -- but adding `export const onRequestError = Sentry.captureRequestError`\nwould silence it and is a one-line Sentry config change, deliberately left out\nof a dependency upgrade.\n\nVerified:\n  yarn tsc --noEmit   clean, on TypeScript 4.7.4 (Next 15 does not require TS 5,\n                      unlike i18next 24 which is still blocked for that reason)\n  yarn test           36 tests across 5 files, all passing\n  yarn build          succeeds; 142 warnings, identical to main built with a\n                      cold .next cache; route set unchanged\n  yarn codegen        succeeds\n  smoke test          built app served on all locales -- correct lang attribute,\n                      correct i18n store, translated CTA in the server HTML\n                      (en/nl/fr/de/pl); browser load of /nl/preview hydrates with\n                      ZERO console errors and ZERO warnings, CTA renders as\n                      \"Probeer het uit\"\n\nBundle grows slightly: shared first-load JS 223 kB -> 226 kB, and the two\npatient-facing routes 453 kB -> 455 kB. Expected from the Next 15 runtime.\n\n@next/swc-win32-ia32-msvc leaves the tree (Next 15 dropped 32-bit Windows);\nirrelevant to the linux/amd64 deploy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh2n1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJlcQAC59Yr1RvORTNOdZRgyKWx3t\nh5/OCTip0WNdWqYE/BTQMJc7Pt2b6PvowdfxHCdfUJrSMnCgH6NwRoFOpBAxN2Xf\nsQsKL/TC+eTG1ki6Y4W7ebln0jMm2NvJkKY9CkArrcOinHU5HQ6QIUrigC21RBY6\nQwZZYdvQuzM77Bt0BtGlLImxjN/XLQDtRte0fIieWUXZaRJwwxn01FU9VUalmXyZ\ndm4jH1LuOGk0rOniiU4UDm5Qgu8F//u7q66LhEKJbpTCTLD2QOOIMuPI6L7bLNE5\nIfxmIFIsSnwI6LxT7g8d/lpqDF6IRnKlERapx6sxVcbYr1PujY+1ZcJVpuRF+4XW\nM0AHc1G4lOcYN43GYPccn7qY2XMVt83aak6E3OIoLAAPq3i6SP9yBF9Qo2XGUdFZ\nZ9ZjQc2gZMjDdsgLUyBZOZQ9L82ZDx2fHw4oLJmnWk5SXbTlmDGHPhYr5OHigwdL\nZao3KNvrUgKes2TWRmhlkn5bt0mKLjUyDjZa3LWM+vEnY8pCGcFpyLmhzSnmdG4W\n5yV6JI5aRqOmzFSMXet0SckK1leJGiQYNsg+GBH70cxs42AaMzR0bqmhpajS1VHw\nBC3giFkBmNeMR1UXn96nQpYV5zoJYmaO02KIA8KYM6BjIsWho1ZaTmHHFb9FGRlI\nv37fqBhnaWT6bo6AWz5U\n=UH9B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:56:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKDY5NzBhYWJhOTM5ZmMzNDJiZjY2MDM2ZWYxMDI0ZjQyMjI2Yzc3NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a","sha":"632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a"}],"sha":"6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/6970aaba939fc342bf66036ef1024f42226c7765"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:31:07Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:31:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): upgrade jsonwebtoken to 9.x (#444)\n\njsonwebtoken         8.5.1 -> 9.0.3   CVE-2022-23539 (81), CVE-2022-23540 (76)\n  @types/jsonwebtoken  8.5.8 -> 9.0.10  kept in step with the runtime\n\nBumping the direct dependency was not sufficient. A second 8.5.1 copy survived\nunderneath @graphql-tools/prisma-loader@7.2.8, which declares `jsonwebtoken\n^8.5.1`, so Aikido would have kept reporting it. prisma-loader 7.2.72 drops the\njsonwebtoken dependency entirely, and the existing `^7.2.7` descriptor already\nspans it, so re-resolving the parent removes the copy rather than forcing a\nversion into code that still expects v8. No resolution added.\n\nReachability, since it changes how this should be read: both CVEs are about\n`jwt.verify()` -- insecure default algorithm, and insecure key retrieval. This\nrepo never calls verify. All four call sites are `jwt.sign()`:\n\n  pages/api/session/[sessionId].ts\n  pages/api/identity/verify.ts\n  lib/startHostedPathwaySession.ts\n  lib/startHostedActivitySession.ts\n\nall of the same shape, `jwt.sign(payloadObject, <string secret>, { issuer,\nsubject })`. So the advisories were not exploitable here; the upgrade clears the\nfinding and removes the risk of a future verify() call inheriting the old\ndefaults.\n\nBehaviour differential against the version that actually ships, using that exact\ncall shape:\n\n  header + claims          identical (alg HS256, typ JWT; same iss/sub/iat)\n  8.5.1-signed token       accepted by 9.0.3\n  9.0.3-signed token       accepted by 8.5.1\n  undefined/empty secret   both throw \"secretOrPrivateKey must have a value\"\n\nCross-compatibility in both directions matters here: these tokens are minted for\nthe orchestration API, and a rolling deploy will have both versions live at\nonce.\n\nThe lockfile churn is large -- 41 package names -- because lifting prisma-loader\n7.2.8 -> 7.2.72 pulls much of the graphql-tools ecosystem with it, including\ngraphql-request across two majors. All of it sits under @graphql-codegen/cli, a\ndevDependency, and none of it ships. It is verified inert: `yarn codegen`\nproduces byte-identical output on main and on this branch, compared via a\nworktree.\n\n  yarn tsc --noEmit   clean\n  yarn test           36 tests across 5 files, all passing\n  yarn build          succeeds, 142 warnings -- same as main built with a cold\n                      .next cache\n  yarn codegen        succeeds, output identical to main\n\nNote the checked-in files under src/types/generated/ are stale relative to the\nsibling orchestration schema -- running codegen adds CareflowEventsPayload,\nActivityTimerPayload, WebhookCallsPayload and others. That drift predates this\nchange and is deliberately not included here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cc161db9d754eae53cda8012fe975a53a077ce5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/5cc161db9d754eae53cda8012fe975a53a077ce5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a","verification":{"payload":"tree 5cc161db9d754eae53cda8012fe975a53a077ce5\nparent 618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1787257867 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787257867 -0600\n\nfix(security): upgrade jsonwebtoken to 9.x (#444)\n\njsonwebtoken         8.5.1 -> 9.0.3   CVE-2022-23539 (81), CVE-2022-23540 (76)\n  @types/jsonwebtoken  8.5.8 -> 9.0.10  kept in step with the runtime\n\nBumping the direct dependency was not sufficient. A second 8.5.1 copy survived\nunderneath @graphql-tools/prisma-loader@7.2.8, which declares `jsonwebtoken\n^8.5.1`, so Aikido would have kept reporting it. prisma-loader 7.2.72 drops the\njsonwebtoken dependency entirely, and the existing `^7.2.7` descriptor already\nspans it, so re-resolving the parent removes the copy rather than forcing a\nversion into code that still expects v8. No resolution added.\n\nReachability, since it changes how this should be read: both CVEs are about\n`jwt.verify()` -- insecure default algorithm, and insecure key retrieval. This\nrepo never calls verify. All four call sites are `jwt.sign()`:\n\n  pages/api/session/[sessionId].ts\n  pages/api/identity/verify.ts\n  lib/startHostedPathwaySession.ts\n  lib/startHostedActivitySession.ts\n\nall of the same shape, `jwt.sign(payloadObject, <string secret>, { issuer,\nsubject })`. So the advisories were not exploitable here; the upgrade clears the\nfinding and removes the risk of a future verify() call inheriting the old\ndefaults.\n\nBehaviour differential against the version that actually ships, using that exact\ncall shape:\n\n  header + claims          identical (alg HS256, typ JWT; same iss/sub/iat)\n  8.5.1-signed token       accepted by 9.0.3\n  9.0.3-signed token       accepted by 8.5.1\n  undefined/empty secret   both throw \"secretOrPrivateKey must have a value\"\n\nCross-compatibility in both directions matters here: these tokens are minted for\nthe orchestration API, and a rolling deploy will have both versions live at\nonce.\n\nThe lockfile churn is large -- 41 package names -- because lifting prisma-loader\n7.2.8 -> 7.2.72 pulls much of the graphql-tools ecosystem with it, including\ngraphql-request across two majors. All of it sits under @graphql-codegen/cli, a\ndevDependency, and none of it ships. It is verified inert: `yarn codegen`\nproduces byte-identical output on main and on this branch, compared via a\nworktree.\n\n  yarn tsc --noEmit   clean\n  yarn test           36 tests across 5 files, all passing\n  yarn build          succeeds, 142 warnings -- same as main built with a cold\n                      .next cache\n  yarn codegen        succeeds, output identical to main\n\nNote the checked-in files under src/types/generated/ are stale relative to the\nsibling orchestration schema -- running codegen adds CareflowEventsPayload,\nActivityTimerPayload, WebhookCallsPayload and others. That drift predates this\nchange and is deliberately not included here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh2QLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAohgQACHzZc9Er7CKSNg64Gv5E8GK\n9f516xLb9YravBVz4J3KQEiXjX6sbsl7SMosOcnx774Jf4+6hO55TIeC/FFjjWYk\nuN0iOql6XX8YM0E06gpUZqD2siHS8cZfH24LhvINF3+FVr0G9hgCt32+Vt8boiYf\neTKuUfVc5iiJUpdw3kl4fA6cAwt7UmLdlBnRWaVDMdwh1YnSsPP5H7O1sqjeo7Yu\nNQ96zcYVL8oT0oabJwcQ1zcAlBCJa9d5DaHQYSE5WR/0CzHGf/EZdDsaDA/VFvNR\nqTgHlw/yhIocVjXOv+7o0toLl7Yx6t9l1s6ZF6U9QK1zcqJ+BwvZhSuFh78BLip0\n4g6SK5PlA9FwJf2U2FIZgoy/PB3NHTlWjQikEDWGviMIRfchoIV+5fd80wzLAGX0\naMzIZY+3xrqJgnodv43iuH77YkbnMfUmN0FBzxkKqiRFn4N7cVIfLa3pPNCOOyHc\nlnXrcXG65uTcle/eJfYRP2W8QaJgBJtGugZ9iAvwf9XhLDS7o22sUt2DrWW74cGr\n8YZFqxMzxQxdMAGGznEU3IMTDn7rnXS6B5QMoSkpZ1xkVNSJjLAX5KuNeDFdC9Dd\nN2lJUeSmeZKUKwEplN5sGG/uvo+zbZV7gJIuZHXxH0jAj4dNnroyvykgHXqt2ZMW\n/9mdp9dX8fF1aQkEdzya\n=qDX1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:31:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKDYzMmU3YjY5NTg5MmI1MTdmYjM0MDk5NjZkOTA0ODQ3YWE5YzQ4MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a","sha":"618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a"}],"sha":"632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/632e7b695892b517fb3409966d904847aa9c481a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:16:42Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:16:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): clear axios, jws and qs highs (#443)\n\naxios  1.15.2 -> 1.19.0   AIKIDO-2026-291630 (75), GHSA-hcpx-6fm6-wx23 (69)\n  jws    4.0.0  -> 4.0.1    CVE-2025-65945 (76)\n         3.2.2  -> 3.2.3    same CVE, second copy Aikido does not report\n  qs     6.12.1 -> 6.15.3   CVE-2026-2391 (75)\n\naxios was not blocked by a range. It was pinned to 1.15.2 by an entry in\n`resolutions`, added in #418 (2026-05-07) as \"update axios from 1.7.7 to\n1.15.2\" -- a correct security fix at the time that has since inverted and was\nholding a vulnerable version down. axios is not a direct dependency; its only\nreal descriptor is `^1.7.7`, which already reaches 1.18.0. So the entry is\nremoved rather than re-pinned, which is one fewer pin to maintain.\n\njws and qs needed no manifest change: `^3.2.2`, `^4.0.0` and `^6.11.0` all\nalready spanned their fixes.\n\nYarn 1 has no equivalent of `yarn up -R`, and `yarn upgrade <name>` is a no-op\nfor packages that are not in package.json -- it reported \"Saved 0 new\ndependencies\" and changed nothing. The working approach is to drop the relevant\nblocks from yarn.lock and let `yarn install` re-resolve them to the highest\nversion each existing range allows. No version was written by hand.\n\nCo-moving transitives are confined to these three families: jwa 1.4.1 -> 1.4.2\nand 2.0.0 -> 2.0.1 (jws), hasown / object-inspect / side-channel /\nside-channel-list (qs), and form-data 4.0.5 -> 4.0.6 (axios) -- the last of\nwhich is itself the patched version for CVE-2026-12143.\n\nVerified: `yarn build` succeeds and typechecks.\n\nBuild warnings are unchanged. An earlier comparison appeared to show 139 -> 142\nand that was wrong: the 139 baseline had been produced with a warm .next cache,\nso ESLint reported a subset of files. Rebuilt both sides with the cache removed\nand both produce 142. The four \"new\" warnings were all no-unused-vars on\nfirst-party constants, which this change does not touch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fdfbdfbf8e3c830b5a418fff7ff435a3743e4c57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/fdfbdfbf8e3c830b5a418fff7ff435a3743e4c57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a","verification":{"payload":"tree fdfbdfbf8e3c830b5a418fff7ff435a3743e4c57\nparent 225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1787257002 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787257002 -0600\n\nfix(security): clear axios, jws and qs highs (#443)\n\naxios  1.15.2 -> 1.19.0   AIKIDO-2026-291630 (75), GHSA-hcpx-6fm6-wx23 (69)\n  jws    4.0.0  -> 4.0.1    CVE-2025-65945 (76)\n         3.2.2  -> 3.2.3    same CVE, second copy Aikido does not report\n  qs     6.12.1 -> 6.15.3   CVE-2026-2391 (75)\n\naxios was not blocked by a range. It was pinned to 1.15.2 by an entry in\n`resolutions`, added in #418 (2026-05-07) as \"update axios from 1.7.7 to\n1.15.2\" -- a correct security fix at the time that has since inverted and was\nholding a vulnerable version down. axios is not a direct dependency; its only\nreal descriptor is `^1.7.7`, which already reaches 1.18.0. So the entry is\nremoved rather than re-pinned, which is one fewer pin to maintain.\n\njws and qs needed no manifest change: `^3.2.2`, `^4.0.0` and `^6.11.0` all\nalready spanned their fixes.\n\nYarn 1 has no equivalent of `yarn up -R`, and `yarn upgrade <name>` is a no-op\nfor packages that are not in package.json -- it reported \"Saved 0 new\ndependencies\" and changed nothing. The working approach is to drop the relevant\nblocks from yarn.lock and let `yarn install` re-resolve them to the highest\nversion each existing range allows. No version was written by hand.\n\nCo-moving transitives are confined to these three families: jwa 1.4.1 -> 1.4.2\nand 2.0.0 -> 2.0.1 (jws), hasown / object-inspect / side-channel /\nside-channel-list (qs), and form-data 4.0.5 -> 4.0.6 (axios) -- the last of\nwhich is itself the patched version for CVE-2026-12143.\n\nVerified: `yarn build` succeeds and typechecks.\n\nBuild warnings are unchanged. An earlier comparison appeared to show 139 -> 142\nand that was wrong: the 139 baseline had been produced with a warm .next cache,\nso ESLint reported a subset of files. Rebuilt both sides with the cache removed\nand both produce 142. The four \"new\" warnings were all no-unused-vars on\nfirst-party constants, which this change does not touch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh2CqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2skQAGblWzp7FBKe4JtTpZ4y8SCd\n7Pxv1JB4Na4J1QzL22MjWR9teKFmuYR8OCNVh7H2eit5VSxqfUDMDDZWKWl6lkCM\nwUMkKNHbigZgrxREh/QwS59Ts/RPc4qGrYXhiu6rmIy+YtqRsUn2sPTbnMPW0GFI\nHDrRJp+qizVEcMcUYSpdieWH4pCl+LRSbar72E2Jb0VUklJUKboY7FSgh4U5oaOl\n/YWIYaUwImUtAV2DxUMtORJ8O9+fgNWM5UrznkXq3guj/eVdi9iJNKoWj2D6JMit\nbK8afcN/7tpl3Al/+uKH0x0hnT0InKe1r4Z6DUWJSLiXjZh3wXdnhQ8XcZNYpaFk\nyCrt9wPGdnBoa8RAdyIbyS5V/Yz7iwSGjr6pW/Jv0YUiZJpCvSoRGaNbSGJk5Dcj\nYGdUtk4RCp6sg+tRP73eWPCagA9eHeaBYsMH/tVi58V+R4szeyVhwT55ABzZsNe3\nqDeHEm2ReCYT11F46f/mtyf1mlgdroBilRdx48pEhROfsJ+8lcoTmJTglHMt/ikk\n6uY8MCs6+1cVZ6ZNSLE6BK6d4Cq9G8lerfQLCskZPBUxZ9/uZw+L/DKVdykOqRyj\ndURc+56AIAwoLAl28mBahO7u6q5VZUod/Acqby50CIEeYQ4E7DjmGMgU+s1LZ8Pi\nZ5mceKctoX+o53YTolAB\n=Rt1k\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:16:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKDYxOGRiYjI3MDliM2NkNWRhMjZhMjE1ZjJjZjdiNmUxZGNiN2NkM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e","sha":"225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e"}],"sha":"618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/618dbb2709b3cd5da26a215f2cf7b6e1dcb7cd3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247668?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mikepack","id":247668,"login":"mikepack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzY2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikepack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:05:30Z","email":"mikepackdev@gmail.com","name":"Mike Pack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:05:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): upgrade next-i18next to clear i18next-fs-backend criticals (#442)\n\ni18next-fs-backend  1.1.4 -> 2.6.7\n    CVE-2026-48713 (91, critical), AIKIDO-2026-10994 (91, critical)\n\ni18next-fs-backend is not a direct dependency; it arrives through next-i18next,\nwhich declared `^1.1.4` -- a caret on 1.x that cannot reach the 2.6.6 fix. The\nonly route is upgrading the parent.\n\n  next-i18next   11.3.0 -> 15.4.3\n  i18next        21.8.16 -> 23.16.8   (now a direct dependency)\n  react-i18next  11.18.3 -> 14.1.3    (now a direct dependency)\n\nnext-i18next 15 moved i18next and react-i18next from `dependencies` to\n`peerDependencies`. Yarn 1 does not install peers, so both have to be declared\ndirectly or they would simply vanish from the tree.\n\nnext-i18next 15.4.3 requires only `next >= 12.0.0` and `react >= 17.0.2`; this\nrepo is on next 14.2.35 and react 18.2.0, so the criticals are fixable without\ntouching Next.js. Chose 15.x over 16.x deliberately: 16 replaces\ni18next-fs-backend with i18next-resources-to-backend, which would mean reworking\nhow locales load rather than upgrading a dependency.\n\nThe API surface is small and unchanged across the jump -- useTranslation (45\ncall sites), serverSideTranslations (4), appWithTranslation, withTranslation.\n\nVerified, since this repo has no tests and no CI gate on pull requests:\n\n  - `yarn build` succeeds and typechecks. Route table is identical to the\n    baseline build on main, and the warning count is unchanged at 139.\n  - `yarn lint` unchanged.\n  - Translations actually load through the upgraded i18next-fs-backend. Ran the\n    real serverSideTranslations call for all nine locales and asserted real\n    strings and intact interpolation:\n        en Submit / de Absenden / es Enviar / et Esita vastused / fr Soumettre\n        nl Verzenden / ro Trimiteți / ru Подать / pl Zatwierdź\n        \"You have uploaded {{count}} files.\" and its translations preserved\n\nNot fixed here, and the reason is measured rather than assumed:\n\n  i18next AIKIDO-2024-10543 (84) needs 24.1.2. i18next 24+ declares\n  `typescript: ^5` and this repo pins typescript 4.7.4. Installing 24 anyway\n  fails the build:\n      ./node_modules/i18next/typescript/t.d.ts:286:5\n      Type error: Type parameter declaration expected.\n  That is TypeScript 5''s `const` type-parameter syntax, which 4.7.4 cannot\n  parse. Clearing that advisory requires upgrading TypeScript first, which is\n  its own change. 23.16.8 is the newest release that works here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2ac5a9bf074f9074a581b67e391b7d244730fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/e2ac5a9bf074f9074a581b67e391b7d244730fb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e","verification":{"payload":"tree e2ac5a9bf074f9074a581b67e391b7d244730fb5\nparent ab995cc610e7d7f5c5ac6b6f7c03e60ef6c2f382\nauthor Mike Pack <mikepackdev@gmail.com> 1787256330 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787256330 -0600\n\nfix(security): upgrade next-i18next to clear i18next-fs-backend criticals (#442)\n\ni18next-fs-backend  1.1.4 -> 2.6.7\n    CVE-2026-48713 (91, critical), AIKIDO-2026-10994 (91, critical)\n\ni18next-fs-backend is not a direct dependency; it arrives through next-i18next,\nwhich declared `^1.1.4` -- a caret on 1.x that cannot reach the 2.6.6 fix. The\nonly route is upgrading the parent.\n\n  next-i18next   11.3.0 -> 15.4.3\n  i18next        21.8.16 -> 23.16.8   (now a direct dependency)\n  react-i18next  11.18.3 -> 14.1.3    (now a direct dependency)\n\nnext-i18next 15 moved i18next and react-i18next from `dependencies` to\n`peerDependencies`. Yarn 1 does not install peers, so both have to be declared\ndirectly or they would simply vanish from the tree.\n\nnext-i18next 15.4.3 requires only `next >= 12.0.0` and `react >= 17.0.2`; this\nrepo is on next 14.2.35 and react 18.2.0, so the criticals are fixable without\ntouching Next.js. Chose 15.x over 16.x deliberately: 16 replaces\ni18next-fs-backend with i18next-resources-to-backend, which would mean reworking\nhow locales load rather than upgrading a dependency.\n\nThe API surface is small and unchanged across the jump -- useTranslation (45\ncall sites), serverSideTranslations (4), appWithTranslation, withTranslation.\n\nVerified, since this repo has no tests and no CI gate on pull requests:\n\n  - `yarn build` succeeds and typechecks. Route table is identical to the\n    baseline build on main, and the warning count is unchanged at 139.\n  - `yarn lint` unchanged.\n  - Translations actually load through the upgraded i18next-fs-backend. Ran the\n    real serverSideTranslations call for all nine locales and asserted real\n    strings and intact interpolation:\n        en Submit / de Absenden / es Enviar / et Esita vastused / fr Soumettre\n        nl Verzenden / ro Trimiteți / ru Подать / pl Zatwierdź\n        \"You have uploaded {{count}} files.\" and its translations preserved\n\nNot fixed here, and the reason is measured rather than assumed:\n\n  i18next AIKIDO-2024-10543 (84) needs 24.1.2. i18next 24+ declares\n  `typescript: ^5` and this repo pins typescript 4.7.4. Installing 24 anyway\n  fails the build:\n      ./node_modules/i18next/typescript/t.d.ts:286:5\n      Type error: Type parameter declaration expected.\n  That is TypeScript 5''s `const` type-parameter syntax, which 4.7.4 cannot\n  parse. Clearing that advisory requires upgrading TypeScript first, which is\n  its own change. 23.16.8 is the newest release that works here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh14KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAItIQAAV2vqz9n82KxZ7IT3gadDH6\nc2dHfIe+DCmIhz8uHZNcihATT9LfMJ1OuK5EUlfeXl6pbLO2h30F1Qog5MwZcsvE\nvCChNGqQ4VWoMosZZVjTgWgaNofsFUjQUrYsZFSwigBtIDMaVBRNCLuDn8FWU8HL\nvDmOietUwHJUK3BL0obLkgcub/Vpy+JjLYRsE03wSlPON55eOMvwXxQ7xZTeWFS5\n///kBByj3m3tS08oUeF2Q83Dtf5pOe1dSWPBU3OtLBuVUMAYO7qkAis3vPdj39xY\nZ6LUAFgJe1LhUuExghNM1Kfq1Tg7EWfHDsqZ0hYrXHjSOTHYB78TTZX5ggbzBh53\nPjoRcbsIpZydqQ0+I/FSPZXBxwZoaExpjesjl71mL48hGHPGApT62CW2jizieLBi\n/uw2zPQUF/vQbWpjWa4V13+EAPUvhnaw+eC1KPkCvTXcaC2Tv/nEHUOGfQ2fVCle\n5uC9+f+il6ZUfpbcMBtBfRKfeoeF2jqD3OWYQUormYIP0QdQqHtQJot5OpLl/yt6\nTLNRfN+GvEkikUGg98gVs4N42Bkefr2Cgn7PB5VhPb6RCzNQ/ind5fbO3mwEPfHk\nECfMnfayynrqVoUFmXZeBwWR0FiTFcHvtkLsH0+f3Imi3Els44hyujP5M3p3nFPV\nwK1VCguq6xWj9ZyNa0km\n=J3RX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T20:05:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKDIyNWYyZGQxYWZiNjZiZDliMjhlZjg4MTIzYTVhZjliNDg5MDI2NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/ab995cc610e7d7f5c5ac6b6f7c03e60ef6c2f382","sha":"ab995cc610e7d7f5c5ac6b6f7c03e60ef6c2f382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/ab995cc610e7d7f5c5ac6b6f7c03e60ef6c2f382"}],"sha":"225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/225f2dd1afb66bd9b28ef88123a5af9b4890265e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56586563?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aran3004","id":56586563,"login":"aran3004","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTg2NTYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aran3004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/ab995cc610e7d7f5c5ac6b6f7c03e60ef6c2f382/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:24:19Z","email":"56586563+aran3004@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aran3004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:24:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add notify-docs workflow (#441)\n\n* ci: add notify-docs workflow\n\nAdd .github/workflows/notify-docs.yml, copied verbatim from\nawell-health/awell-docs/skills/triggering-doc-updates/starter/github-notify-docs.yml.\n\nOn a merged pull request, the workflow POSTs a `doc-update`\nrepository_dispatch event to awell-health/awell-docs so the docs agent\nover there can read the merged change and open a documentation PR for\nreview. Nothing in this repo is gated: no checkout, no build, no status\ncheck, no required block. The workflow fires one dispatch and exits.\n\nA plain HTTPS POST is used instead of a `uses:` reference to a reusable\nworkflow because awell-docs is private and a public repo such as\nhosted-pages cannot call a reusable workflow that lives in a private\nrepo. Any repo can POST to a private repo''s dispatch endpoint with a\ntoken, so this file works everywhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: add Documentation section to CLAUDE.md\n\nDocument the notify-docs workflow''s behaviour for PR authors: nothing\ngates merges, the `docs-skip` label opts a merge out of docs generation\nentirely, and a `[DOCUMENTATION]` block in the PR description is optional\nguidance that steers the docs agent. Point at the awell-docs SKILL.md for\nthe block''s fields and rules.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3206143936ecce78eb6f30380dceb5ed1c8d1d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/e3206143936ecce78eb6f30380dceb5ed1c8d1d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/ab995cc610e7d7f5c5ac6b6f7c03e60ef6c2f382","verification":{"payload":"tree e3206143936ecce78eb6f30380dceb5ed1c8d1d5\nparent 4122f62e1404145a07a84860661a98ab318ada1c\nauthor aran3004 <56586563+aran3004@users.noreply.github.com> 1786465459 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786465459 +0100\n\nci: add notify-docs workflow (#441)\n\n* ci: add notify-docs workflow\n\nAdd .github/workflows/notify-docs.yml, copied verbatim from\nawell-health/awell-docs/skills/triggering-doc-updates/starter/github-notify-docs.yml.\n\nOn a merged pull request, the workflow POSTs a `doc-update`\nrepository_dispatch event to awell-health/awell-docs so the docs agent\nover there can read the merged change and open a documentation PR for\nreview. Nothing in this repo is gated: no checkout, no build, no status\ncheck, no required block. The workflow fires one dispatch and exits.\n\nA plain HTTPS POST is used instead of a `uses:` reference to a reusable\nworkflow because awell-docs is private and a public repo such as\nhosted-pages cannot call a reusable workflow that lives in a private\nrepo. Any repo can POST to a private repo''s dispatch endpoint with a\ntoken, so this file works everywhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: add Documentation section to CLAUDE.md\n\nDocument the notify-docs workflow''s behaviour for PR authors: nothing\ngates merges, the `docs-skip` label opts a merge out of docs generation\nentirely, and a `[DOCUMENTATION]` block in the PR description is optional\nguidance that steers the docs agent. Point at the awell-docs SKILL.md for\nthe block''s fields and rules.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe0y0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlncQAImokbwIZ3lRPADHO6vT98Nh\nP+IRqC+VDS9I8AoVagh2ra7SJJ9UkIBz0Ov85sYy+gykr2L3ynAWkrJ34uuq2Nnq\nc+kVIMLKxzRIdqNNpwjswdNJVMcxY23HbQHSy/0A+xEZyrjs/aUZFH2tAXXXqH2o\n3wEAhWCdilMdhKbqI+bARM41Bp7usHwYxG6T6vzbtJU1r1Z8rtCj4gcHprHfMZfU\n1ovBLSbI9uVoJTqQOY7EbYFDkLly5M73rJQAYjVA5i4rbZBCvdD/BtESdlYaDN9G\n9tDfq4FopqxlPH8D3FGYCL7BhIU413gqf6AoCHPeb1VPBF3noXps2PlqU8c9a3Rj\nnYnJ2XoEHD+IQukGmmHn7MEoepgCwEG13KlM8hmlgtVBguj42KshjVMnnldLraSQ\n810d8NjvNETlt0lVe32L/iPxwWlXmSWcELE0PuS18HSmPwPWaX7U+uS/RPGyDYUK\nY25TwNjuE+wWdaClAPCFUXof40QrAVsbUF0/GiecqCakxiH7vYxt/WHLQ4DgCCYu\nHKlDuEK4rJSttTKfkNV6yfuMGzIrzNYSqMwmzkErg8fvATexI7o/MPNxjS2mj9LP\nce81HfxXVFrh15qV3vaeBTn+r09KjEV5xANjicO7VYU0cP3AmGGiAak2Djy2Z4cr\nCrhdj/hZgFxMiZlP1e+X\n=G0Sj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T16:24:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow