om/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/483f610bc4ab7c2bff1b53561ed2b2f2592d85df","node_id":"C_kwDOHttB09oAKDQ4M2Y2MTBiYzRhYjdjMmJmZjFiNTM1NjFlZDJiMmYyNTkyZDg1ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/awell-health/hosted-pages/commit/a0bf96f82160ad38893e6cf5eff08f49f72cebeb","sha":"a0bf96f82160ad38893e6cf5eff08f49f72cebeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/a0bf96f82160ad38893e6cf5eff08f49f72cebeb"}],"sha":"483f610bc4ab7c2bff1b53561ed2b2f2592d85df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/483f610bc4ab7c2bff1b53561ed2b2f2592d85df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47522087?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ebomcke-awell","id":47522087,"login":"ebomcke-awell","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTIyMDg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ebomcke-awell","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/commits/a0bf96f82160ad38893e6cf5eff08f49f72cebeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-05T16:11:53Z","email":"47522087+ebomcke-awell@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ebomcke-awell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-05T16:11:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Improve hosted sessions observability for customer diagnosis (#391)\n\n* refactor: consolidate logging into single unified utility (AWL-3554)\n\n- Consolidate client and server logging into src/utils/logging.ts\n- Remove unnecessary separation between client/server logging (Sentry handles this)\n- Remove LogSeverity type (redundant with logger.info/warn/error methods)\n- Add LogEvent enum and logger utility in single file\n- Update all imports across codebase to use unified logging\n- Remove log parameter from IntakeScheduling API service (use logger directly)\n- Delete old logging files: serverLogging.ts, sentryLogging.ts, useLogging/types.ts\n\nThis improves observability consistency and reduces code duplication as part of\nthe hosted sessions observability improvements.\n\n* refactor: standardize Sentry error handling and logging (AWL-3554)\n\n- Update HostedSessionError to support level, tags, and contexts properties\n- Create captureHostedSessionError helper to extract metadata from errors\n- Replace all Sentry.captureException calls with HostedSessionError pattern\n- Replace all breadcrumb calls with Sentry.logger calls\n- Remove addSentryBreadcrumb wrapper function (replaced with direct logger calls)\n- Replace captureMessage calls with logger calls\n- Add Sentry reporting to catch blocks that were missing it\n\nAll errors now consistently use HostedSessionError with level/tags/contexts\nset in the error object, ensuring consistent observability across the application.\n\n* Apply observability best practices\n\n- Move logging calls from render functions to useEffect hooks to prevent duplicate logs on re-render\n- Enhance error logging with full error details (error message, name, stack)\n- Update observability rules to clarify that Sentry.logger.error and captureHostedSessionError serve different purposes (structured logging vs error reporting) and are not duplicates\n\n* chore: disable sentry''s maskAllText as we mask explicitly\n\n* Refactor hosted activity session flow to use SSR\n\n- Replace client-side SWR fetching with server-side rendering in getServerSideProps\n- Extract session creation logic to shared server function (lib/startHostedActivitySession.ts)\n- Use union type for return value (Success | Error) instead of optional error field\n- Consolidate error handling: all logging and Sentry reporting in single place\n- Simplify component to render-only (no fetching logic)\n- Remove loading states and client-side redirect logic\n- Show error page as fallback instead of empty fragment\n\n* refactor: convert /c/ page to SSR pattern matching /l/ page\n\n- Create startHostedPathwaySession server-side function in lib/\n- Refactor pages/c/[hostedPagesLinkId].tsx to use GetServerSideProps\n- Remove client-side flow component and NoSSR wrapper\n- Add server-side error handling and redirects\n- Add Sentry logging for successful redirects\n\n* chore: get rid of unused start hosted session component\n\n* chore: apply observability best practices to logging in activities\n\n* fix: validate session_url and fix duplicate logging in AuthenticationProvider\n\n- Add validation for missing session_url in GraphQL responses to prevent invalid redirect URLs\n- Fix duplicate logging in AuthenticationProvider by splitting router and token logs\n- Remove unnecessary ref-based state tracking for logging\n\n* Add organization_slug to Sentry logging and error reporting\n\n- Extract organization_slug from mutation responses in startHostedPathwaySession and startHostedActivitySession\n- Add organization_slug as log attribute in all Sentry.logger calls where available\n- Set organization_slug as Sentry tag and context in useHostedSession when session loads\n- Add organization_slug as tag in error captures for server-side functions (before session scope is available)\n- Remove redundant manual passing of organization_slug in client-side error handlers (rely on Sentry scope)\n- Update return types to include organization_slug for successful session starts\n- Remove deleted StartHostedActivitySessionPayload export from types/index.ts\n\n* feat: automatically record replays for specific organizations\n\n- Configure Sentry replay to buffer by default (replaysOnErrorSampleRate: 1.0)\n- Set replaysSessionSampleRate to 0 for manual control\n- Add automatic replay recording for organizations specified in NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_REPLAY_ORGANIZATIONS env var\n- Separate useEffect hooks with proper dependencies to prevent unnecessary re-runs during polling\n- Replay is flushed/started only when organization_slug changes\n- Sentry context is updated only when session ID changes\n\n* feat: enable selective masking of content for sentry\n\n- mask everyting inside the activity container and leave everything else\nunmasked\n\n* feat: improve sentry errors\n\n- use safe serialisation function when logging subscription errors\n- remove duplicate error reports for failures in hosted session and\nhosted session activities queries\n\n* Switch from Sentry scope to session storage for log context\n\n- Replace getSessionContextFromScope() with getLogAttributesFromSessionStore()\n- Logger now reads session context from sessionStorage.getItem(''log-context'')\n- Remove explicit session context parameters from all logger calls\n- Clean up imports and remove unused session dependencies\n- Use serializeError() consistently for error logging","tree":{"sha":"45446eb6f491170251baa4a275c2d4ead480024f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/trees/45446eb6f491170251baa4a275c2d4ead480024f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/awell-health/hosted-pages/git/commits/a0bf96f82160ad38893e6cf5eff08f49f72cebeb","verification":{"payload":"tree 45446eb6f491170251baa4a275c2d4ead480024f\nparent 5abefd962c4f85bf61f537a34233e9c408015852\nauthor ebomcke-awell <47522087+ebomcke-awell@users.noreply.github.com> 1764951113 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1764951113 +0100\n\nImprove hosted sessions observability for customer diagnosis (#391)\n\n* refactor: consolidate logging into single unified utility (AWL-3554)\n\n- Consolidate client and server logging into src/utils/logging.ts\n- Remove unnecessary separation between client/server logging (Sentry handles this)\n- Remove LogSeverity type (redundant with logger.info/warn/error methods)\n- Add LogEvent enum and logger utility in single file\n- Update all imports across codebase to use unified logging\n- Remove log parameter from IntakeScheduling API service (use logger directly)\n- Delete old logging files: serverLogging.ts, sentryLogging.ts, useLogging/types.ts\n\nThis improves observability consistency and reduces code duplication as part of\nthe hosted sessions observability improvements.\n\n* refactor: standardize Sentry error handling and logging (AWL-3554)\n\n- Update HostedSessionError to support level, tags, and contexts properties\n- Create captureHostedSessionError helper to extract metadata from errors\n- Replace all Sentry.captureException calls with HostedSessionError pattern\n- Replace all breadcrumb calls with Sentry.logger calls\n- Remove addSentryBreadcrumb wrapper function (replaced with direct logger calls)\n- Replace captureMessage calls with logger calls\n- Add Sentry reporting to catch blocks that were missing it\n\nA