nipl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/danipl","id":1307980,"login":"danipl","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDc5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danipl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/d6a0fbcd59e892dda9efc415733bbea61a0e5edc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:19:19Z","email":"daniplst@gmail.com","name":"Daniel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:19:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: wait for tempo-init to finish before starting Tempo [INBOX-362] (#10901)\n\nWith tracing turned on, `invoke dev.start --wait` exited with a\nnon-zero code. Docker Compose `--wait` counts a container that exits\nas a failure, unless another service waits for it with\n`condition: service_completed_successfully`. `infrahub-tempo` listed\n`infrahub-tempo-init` without a condition, so the normal exit of the\ninit container failed the command.\n\nAdd the condition to `infrahub-tempo`, and regenerate the standalone\nobservability Compose file. Tempo now also starts only after the\nowner of its data folder is set.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Pardo <Daniel@OpsAdmins-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79ca82e9f9d7fe00341da3638dd48508c95cff61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/79ca82e9f9d7fe00341da3638dd48508c95cff61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/d6a0fbcd59e892dda9efc415733bbea61a0e5edc","verification":{"payload":"tree 79ca82e9f9d7fe00341da3638dd48508c95cff61\nparent 01b327448b0181888d31ea6737c23cd329d30663\nauthor Daniel <daniplst@gmail.com> 1791274759 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791274759 +0200\n\nfix: wait for tempo-init to finish before starting Tempo [INBOX-362] (#10901)\n\nWith tracing turned on, `invoke dev.start --wait` exited with a\nnon-zero code. Docker Compose `--wait` counts a container that exits\nas a failure, unless another service waits for it with\n`condition: service_completed_successfully`. `infrahub-tempo` listed\n`infrahub-tempo-init` without a condition, so the normal exit of the\ninit container failed the command.\n\nAdd the condition to `infrahub-tempo`, and regenerate the standalone\nobservability Compose file. Tempo now also starts only after the\nowner of its data folder is set.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Pardo <Daniel@OpsAdmins-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxK8HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvvgQAATU5hYJnH5xoxFlwK9bW7Pl\nE518cosihfpDT0XzIeem5rkjA5Ovp/jS9TGeDE0TTz9uCfCCJY6f14PIEzgvj+OE\nHlfDKCUD5c1UErf0zhJRYRgzljFAC55TmgQGMxRMUAZ2dW815xdXWt7loZKFW3iJ\nG+VX/YqwOEB6lyuh4vDdlG3tBcQNhgViDPyTCilD6TP12I+ecZZVO5fqYFxLwIkt\nh23IZrMs5skBW8jKV9w3wX1rW6iWVCGyw0JnkQlbY9dwKcZls7IjTYbasby3jcKV\n7xLsocO3XVw6pLsqFnB8lE0zpesWxWQblQdAe8q0GZF7IiQdcr9pK+f5J9cyqlI6\nQ8L0yt5EWsT0OdJQO6J++wcrg5zA5PYNHvj3YRHBZgI28WXN6Tmn0CY4mb3cL1FD\nAl3+vPG3+HYA+Dw2MaYR4lyxUv6h3Y6L3Yzvg4lJGwvGYz/eR2g4tFxeEE6lVHS5\n9csT/ADH1dYYMyZnQV9k/Ioi5jrDYupPEuk0zbSFTRAenLBkvZR6PDKYDEGlMToa\nYnuOcvyUqdOo43ReieB7aMmaddjrLPIAggKkKC7gH/0p6YeuwkPNPuS4FdRdQQ2O\n7inmUIKgVFrixx/LnmGIxtXX+6NT+59ETkagvjfJYMtWPR+IItY7xvXVBTtJzyeI\n4mod7T+11uWuS8c2EXOK\n=T1ce\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T08:19:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://ap