":"https://api.github.com/users/ogenstad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogenstad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogenstad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogenstad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a32df2c4759bc6ac309d84de27758531bd17471e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:50:26Z","email":"patrick@ogenstad.com","name":"Patrick Ogenstad"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:50:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(git): delete removed definitions after their dependents [IFC-2967] (#10822)\n\n* fix(git): delete removed definitions after their dependents [IFC-2967]\n\nThe repository import deleted stale objects in create order, so removing a\nquery together with the transform or generator definition using it hit the\nmandatory query relationship, aborted the import and left the repository\nstuck on the old commit.\n\nThe import now creates and updates every category first, then deletes the\nnodes the repository no longer declares in reverse dependency order:\ngenerator and check definitions, transforms, queries. Removing the last\nremaining query now deletes it too.\n\nRelates to #10109\n\n* chore(changelog): record the import delete-order fix without closing its issue\n\n* chore(changelog): use the branded terms for Transformations and Generators\n\n* chore(changelog): link the import delete-order fix to its issue again","tree":{"sha":"7389f2bcd95e13f5837473d5aa166fefb92b8c40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/7389f2bcd95e13f5837473d5aa166fefb92b8c40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/a32df2c4759bc6ac309d84de27758531bd17471e","verification":{"payload":"tree 7389f2bcd95e13f5837473d5aa166fefb92b8c40\nparent 3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a\nauthor Patrick Ogenstad <patrick@ogenstad.com> 1791208226 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791208226 +0200\n\nfix(git): delete removed definitions after their dependents [IFC-2967] (#10822)\n\n* fix(git): delete removed definitions after their dependents [IFC-2967]\n\nThe repository import deleted stale objects in create order, so removing a\nquery together with the transform or generator definition using it hit the\nmandatory query relationship, aborted the import and left the repository\nstuck on the old commit.\n\nThe import now creates and updates every category first, then deletes the\nnodes the repository no longer declares in reverse dependency order:\ngenerator and check definitions, transforms, queries. Removing the last\nremaining query now deletes it too.\n\nRelates to #10109\n\n* chore(changelog): record the import delete-order fix without closing its issue\n\n* chore(changelog): use the branded terms for Transformations and Generators\n\n* chore(changelog): link the import delete-order fix to its issue again","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6siCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASL8QAI9lQntMtEuqnE474aMXX0G6\nJAk1EjrRspl7AdM5ZJtfw1HNTUmR++2tuk2Xod2545GHYMklPYp2BNOxClEmRFdu\nQc7JnGkv+wkx8iKV1LLOvdTh33UsJlSN79b4kLEJktRzyhMucDv1o87xqty2kQwc\n27Jihjsxgk1RmFW+R4RmAD+PlZJLUuCdZ29i/Zf3drduXXzyN+qoeAE0T657ZJTx\n04ugVP7PZoM8aX5AYHQqj4PMElczLiwc9z081EX+NsnPVjmnNHEXsMnEbkrBMEL9\n2i3gPm5qPDswnAozUZbmH7f588Per0PAwkrPERH50JYM6F2navGSIlVLh2syJfz1\ntdgzkO3AzptvyAlAIo4BgWuYFWOZ8I6r/5bCxQlkxF7GTPskO2m0nOodqjArRpT4\ncQHzpYhsEKwL10fYbOzDWgIUMtLeJb785MBb3p663xCTYaZtHNETqPJbsynCOtf0\ny9KZ6pUA6CaAtuptdSZntfFFWSeMVn6QrD0l1i3B1McPF+gw+dHRwvvR7lqoL24Y\n6qFi1yd6M+InQsLbjel9B/SOgjUiUvK61/OW2WrA7ACs1347hrzKHcC8K/oiPLJZ\npXu/rnAkvcbQ3zyD7W6CPCDwMd/Z8u5N4l9S9ptP3SUzKBTvFF/x5RAn4nD8x6QI\n3BEJ05gHJI7trkWm+etO\n=PR6s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:50:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a32df2c4759bc6ac309d84de27758531bd17471e","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGEzMmRmMmM0NzU5YmM2YWMzMDlkODRkZTI3NzU4NTMxYmQxNzQ3MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a","sha":"3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a"}],"sha":"a32df2c4759bc6ac309d84de27758531bd17471e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a32df2c4759bc6ac309d84de27758531bd17471e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:33:11Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:35:47Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"test(changelog): build the removed relationship''s peer without random properties\n\nThe factory fills a peer''s properties with random values, and an\nis_protected property holding a random string fails the boolean\nconversion the collector applies. That hit about 8% of builds (33 of\n400), failing test_changelog_of_a_relationship_missing_from_the_schema\nfor a reason unrelated to the unknown peer kind it checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ace828865b38856cd5a9e8d104571b376ed23a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/8ace828865b38856cd5a9e8d104571b376ed23a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDNlYzFjNGE0ZWNlNTQ0ZTA3NWUwMWZlODI2ZmRmY2QzZGRmM2Q1NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/6a1f2952cd21176a5ade8f71b41101cdcefcfece","sha":"6a1f2952cd21176a5ade8f71b41101cdcefcfece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/6a1f2952cd21176a5ade8f71b41101cdcefcfece"}],"sha":"3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3ec1c4a4ece544e075e01fe826fdfcd3ddf3d54a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/455140?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mvanhorn","id":455140,"login":"mvanhorn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTE0MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mvanhorn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/6a1f2952cd21176a5ade8f71b41101cdcefcfece/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:06:00Z","email":"mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Van Horn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:06:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: avoid duplicate HFID constraints with reordered fields (#10810)\n\n* fix: avoid duplicate HFID constraints with reordered fields\n\nFixes #10793\n\n* test: trim the HFID constraint order tests\n\nCover the reordered match with three cases on the existing\ncar_person_schema_root fixture: the same fields reordered, a subset,\nand a superset, so the match stays exact. The changelog now notes that\na schema which already has the duplicate constraint loses it the next\ntime that node''s schema is loaded.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Van Horn <455140+mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"510168b04ae8c81b44a6c6cbfbcde0fdd01efa7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/510168b04ae8c81b44a6c6cbfbcde0fdd01efa7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/6a1f2952cd21176a5ade8f71b41101cdcefcfece","verification":{"payload":"tree 510168b04ae8c81b44a6c6cbfbcde0fdd01efa7b\nparent a62f3378b86f1f649c38434dcb92dc7218aacb18\nauthor Matt Van Horn <mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com> 1791108360 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791108360 +0200\n\nfix: avoid duplicate HFID constraints with reordered fields (#10810)\n\n* fix: avoid duplicate HFID constraints with reordered fields\n\nFixes #10793\n\n* test: trim the HFID constraint order tests\n\nCover the reordered match with three cases on the existing\ncar_person_schema_root fixture: the same fields reordered, a subset,\nand a superset, so the match stays exact. The changelog now notes that\na schema which already has the duplicate constraint loses it the next\ntime that node''s schema is loaded.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Van Horn <455140+mvanhorn@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwiUICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA19wQAAJGfEeVVm89QY7sws9D4xdS\ncDJ1eeWh6MEoxuzJdOhl+MMicRj9JF4433Ke2ln8n8j9UXxTe0NwweFq4zVunKdI\n9IAnGT/OJ5pEMBMr+eyrsVE2+y09OVuE3VSdk8WXKoxQQhC46eKHS1Mafu3wO37a\nKIwwTev2ayBeSNugGLpmDWqBVDEGA4YwkJ4FIsMKWW8QsAq/MFSCDqFOHzWAYMyu\noRaocOE9U86ma3eq6UWTcFHk4ojOzrohCz/D/57m0+B/Gap3PBPQqP5iFoi7uMor\nFB0w9o/eJgw3NnBITw0HTSUy26c1lyRN2d0QSYXZjqYRLmdggWPUa+azucD193OW\nvrN62iqri6Dfi6f+NGbUBKVaGpUrl1uMrcwHLSWjA8H/D/dpL5cBIEKx9WH9GsiA\nY2r9T05BcFkMJoGTM+WgSFXlgVkgfATip5f0Hju7Dpo2e+sjdZZlfEbRjGeBRBSA\ngoZGag5cQPuQMP70TtKXJucKjnGZ538zBOz1nmN3iHWXLL4qcw2nZMp1L3tIemO6\ngsFldkf+mqxD59ooS+1ZTYuIbp6HN8Vl2Akno/uvhvPm2I5GhhfgtmyQ9