in":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/5846548a35c731797119159023ae52c3b7f3c44e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:21:03Z","email":"simon@opsmill.com","name":"Simon AURA--SCUSSEL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:26:54Z","email":"simon.aurascussel+git@gmail.com","name":"Simon AURA--SCUSSEL"},"message":"fix(git): restore a modified artifact file when that artifact is regenerated\n\nRegeneration keeps the stored file when the rendered content is unchanged,\nso Re-generate on an artifact whose stored file was modified or removed\nreported success and left the file refused.\n\nA regeneration of given artifacts, which Re-generate on the artifact page\nand artifact_generate in the SDK request, now reads back the stored file of\neach artifact whose content is unchanged. When that file is missing or\nrefused, or does not match the checksum, it is stored again. Regenerating a\nwhole artifact definition and the automatic regenerations keep the stored\nfiles as they are, with no extra read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon AURA--SCUSSEL <simon@opsmill.com>","tree":{"sha":"e93f104d7809152a9e4201a80ec61daa0890d968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/e93f104d7809152a9e4201a80ec61daa0890d968"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/5846548a35c731797119159023ae52c3b7f3c44e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176209175?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DharmaBytesX","id":176209175,"login":"DharmaBytesX","node_id":"U_kgDOCoC9Fw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/5846548a35c731797119159023ae52c3b7f3c44e","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDU4NDY1NDhhMzVjNzMxNzk3MTE5MTU5MDIzYWU1MmMzYjdmM2M0NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b","sha":"c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b"}],"sha":"5846548a35c731797119159023ae52c3b7f3c44e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/5846548a35c731797119159023ae52c3b7f3c44e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176209175?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DharmaBytesX","id":176209175,"login":"DharmaBytesX","node_id":"U_kgDOCoC9Fw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:58:22Z","email":"simon@opsmill.com","name":"Simon AURA--SCUSSEL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:26:54Z","email":"simon.aurascussel+git@gmail.com","name":"Simon AURA--SCUSSEL"},"message":"fix(api): refuse to serve an artifact file that does not match its checksum\n\nAn artifact file modified in the object storage was served as it was, so the\nweb interface showed it and clients such as the SDK could push it to devices.\n\nReading an artifact file now compares it with the checksum recorded for the\nartifact. A file that does not match is not served: the storage and artifact\nendpoints return a 409 whose message asks to regenerate the artifact, and the\nserver logs a warning. Reading never triggers a regeneration.\n\nThe artifact endpoint compares the file with the artifact''s own checksum and\nrefuses an artifact that records no checksum. The storage endpoint only\nreceives the storage id, so it looks up the checksums artifacts recorded with\nit, on any branch and at any time, pairing each with the storage id recorded\non the same branch at the same time. Content that no artifact records a\nchecksum for is served as before, and a missing file is still a 404.\n\nThe check is on by default. Setting INFRAHUB_STORAGE_VERIFY_ARTIFACT_CHECKSUM\nto false on the API servers turns it off.\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon AURA--SCUSSEL <simon@opsmill.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a1a695101f47efa3d0c54e15fddd785741dd90d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/9a1a695101f47efa3d0c54e15fddd785741dd90d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176209175?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DharmaBytesX","id":176209175,"login":"DharmaBytesX","node_id":"U_kgDOCoC9Fw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGMyY2Q0Y2Y4MmY5MzRlNjAzNWMzZWJiODFhNDE4NTNlM2VkYTNmOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c","sha":"7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c"}],"sha":"c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c2cd4cf82f934e6035c3ebb81a41853e3eda3f9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176209175?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DharmaBytesX","id":176209175,"login":"DharmaBytesX","node_id":"U_kgDOCoC9Fw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:58:33Z","email":"simon@opsmill.com","name":"Simon AURA--SCUSSEL"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:30:12Z","email":"simon.aurascussel+git@gmail.com","name":"Simon AURA--SCUSSEL"},"message":"fix(frontend): show why an artifact or file could not be loaded\n\nThe artifact and file viewers threw the raw REST error body, which is not\nan Error, so they showed \"Sorry, no data found.\" instead of the reason the\nserver returned, for example a file missing from the object storage. They\nnow throw an Error carrying the first message of the REST error body, with\na generic message when the body has none, and show it with the error icon,\ncentred at a readable width.\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon AURA--SCUSSEL <simon@opsmill.com>","tree":{"sha":"f906206e0aca4c7ad6bf0bb0d1656432030882a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/f906206e0aca4c7ad6bf0bb0d1656432030882a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176209175?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DharmaBytesX","id":176209175,"login":"DharmaBytesX","node_id":"U_kgDOCoC9Fw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DharmaBytesX","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDdjMjdiY2NhMGE3ZDk2Mzg5MWI2YmU1ZDk2OTExYmVhMTZlMjBkMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49","sha":"305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49"}],"sha":"7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7c27bcca0a7d963891b6be5d96911bea16e20d1c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:03:14Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:57Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(git): clone over a copy a failed concurrent clone left broken\n\nThe re-check under the repository lock only treated an absent copy as\nneeding a clone. A concurrent clone that failed part-way (the clone\nsucceeded but the checkout did not) leaves a copy that exists but no\nlonger validates, so the waiting flow raised instead of cloning again,\nfailing alongside the one that actually broke. The webhook, branch\ncreate, branch delete, merge and proposed-change conflict paths have no\nfallback for that error.\n\nTreat a broken copy found under the lock like an absent one, and close\nthe Repo the check opened on it first: once the directory is replaced it\nwould keep reading the deleted object store. The check before the lock\nstill raises on a broken copy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a18b1fcac8d81cc3880f82589970213d06f6976","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/8a18b1fcac8d81cc3880f82589970213d06f6976"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDMwNWVkYTEwMzQ3MGY1NDU2YjQ3ODA2ZjYzN2Y1YTM2NjRhZGRiNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886","sha":"3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886"}],"sha":"305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/305eda103470f5456b47806f637f5a3664addb49"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T13:28:33Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:57Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(git): clone a repository under the repository lock\n\nCreating the local copy deletes whatever is at the repository directory before\ncloning into it, and ran outside the repository lock. A periodic sync and a\nrefresh request landing together on one worker therefore both cloned, the second\nwiping the directory the first had just built and invalidating the git objects\nalready opened against it. The sync could then no longer resolve a commit, and\nbroadcast a repository refresh with no commit pinned.\n\nClone under the lock and re-check once it is held, so the flow that loses the\nrace adopts the winner''s clone instead of deleting it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d32f8255174dbe4e44a2fadf88f3b8a9a933874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/8d32f8255174dbe4e44a2fadf88f3b8a9a933874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDNhMTVmMjY3ZDEyNDQxYzhmYzA0YTYyYmE5NTUwYWNjZWI3ZWY4ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2","sha":"bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2"}],"sha":"3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3a15f267d12441c8fc04a62ba9550acceb7ef886"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:53:58Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix: page backfill node ids in uuid order, not the schema order_by\n\nThe whole-kind backfills submit each chunk while later pages are still\nbeing read by offset. When the kind''s order_by sorts on the attribute\nbeing recomputed, the submitted flows rewrite the sort key mid-paging and\nshift nodes across page boundaries, so some are processed twice and\nothers never. Disable ordering in the node id query so pages follow the\nnode uuid alone, which no recompute changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9318a8f2741e05c5c4071ef8d01304097859c3a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/9318a8f2741e05c5c4071ef8d01304097859c3a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGJiMjAwNGFkMjEzMmQwMjM3Zjg0ODkyMDU3OGM0YzgzNDczNDZmYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3","sha":"08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3"}],"sha":"bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/bb2004ad2132d0237f848920578c4c8347346fb2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:51:31Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix: read only node ids when backfilling Python computed attributes\n\nThe whole-kind Python computed attribute recompute loaded every node of\nthe kind through the SDK, with all its attributes, to read `.id`, and held\nthem all in memory before submitting the first batch. Page through the\nnode ids instead, the same way the Jinja2, display label and HFID\nbackfills do, and submit each chunk as it arrives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6707a0108b3cdded47a29760c403ede334adfd5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/6707a0108b3cdded47a29760c403ede334adfd5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDA4Zjg2YTgwNzAwMWI4MmNhNTlhM2FmOTAwMWMzODkyYjkzMzljYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9","sha":"a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9"}],"sha":"08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/08f86a807001b82ca59a3af9001c3892b9339cc3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:04:23Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"test: page backfill node ids two at a time in the chunking tests\n\nThe default pagination size returned all three nodes in one page, so the\nbackfill trigger tests never read a second page. With a pagination size\nof 2 the ids come from two pages; a paging loop that stops after its\nfirst page now fails these tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b8c61a9564b89c889b42138f263001001fbb7d57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/b8c61a9564b89c889b42138f263001001fbb7d57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGE0ZWMxNTFmOTdkNmQwNDJlYmMwMDgxYTM2NjMxODMxMzhmODQ5Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411","sha":"3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411"}],"sha":"a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a4ec151f97d6d042ebc0081a3663183138f849f9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:32:52Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix: skip a node whose template fails to render instead of failing its batch\n\nA backfill flow now renders up to one submission chunk of nodes, so a\nsingle render error (arithmetic or a filter on a null value) dropped the\nupdates of every other node in the chunk; the merge and rebase recompute\nhad the same exposure. The display-label and Jinja2 process flows now log\nthe node and keep its stored value, and write the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7cf1d9aa0b810942e9b60281a53fbf8f7f8c9d3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/7cf1d9aa0b810942e9b60281a53fbf8f7f8c9d3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDNhNjk2MTgzOWFiYTY4OTA0MmIxNWQ3NDNiZmQzZGQ1MjM4OTc0MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25","sha":"37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25"}],"sha":"3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3a6961839aba689042b15d743bfd3dd523897411"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:28:11Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs: compare the chunked backfill to the merge and rebase recompute\n\nThe rebase on this branch does not replay a whole kind; it recomputes\nonly the nodes in the default-branch changelog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3fabbc95eeb8fbc84a9de613e1a5c62f1e27ce77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/3fabbc95eeb8fbc84a9de613e1a5c62f1e27ce77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDM3NDc4YTkyYzllYmE0OGMwZTdkOTQ0NzRlZTFmMTk1MjA3OTVlMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f","sha":"f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f"}],"sha":"37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/37478a92c9eba48c0e7d94474ee1f19520795e25"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:19:48Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs: address review nitpicks on the chunked backfill\n\nUpdate the process_jinja2 docstring now that object_ids is not only a\nmerge/rebase input, shorten the changelog entry, and document that the\nrecompute-all mutation also goes through the chunked backfill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b306c76908bb49963107ffc84c510b76d97bf8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/7b306c76908bb49963107ffc84c510b76d97bf8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGYyMTM5MjVjNDA4MDk4ZGQ1NWM1Y2JkYjNlYjc1ODIyM2JhNDE4OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c","sha":"9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c"}],"sha":"f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/f213925c408098dd55c5cbdb3eb758223ba4189f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:36:51Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix: fetch backfill node ids at the pagination size, keep chunk-sized flows\n\nThe backfill fetched node ids one submission chunk (250) at a time, so a\n151k-node kind took ~600 offset-paginated id queries. Fetch at the client''s\npagination size instead, never below one chunk, and split each page into\nchunk-sized flows.\n\nLab runs on a 151k-interface backup (4 servers, 8 workers, pagination size\n1000), same merge each time:\n- ids fetched at the pagination size, 250-id flows: 5 min 41 s, Neo4j\n  11.0 / 14.2 cores avg / p95, API reads +0.15 s avg.\n- one flow per 1000-id page: 5 min 04 s, same Neo4j load, worse max API\n  read latency (4.07 s vs 2.85 s); the chunk size keeps bounding the flows.\n- ids fetched 250 at a time: 23 min 52 s, but that run also recomputed\n  every other kind, so it is not a clean baseline.\n\nThe floor keeps a small pagination size (50 by default) from shrinking the\nflows to 50 ids, which would submit 5x more flows than a chunk-sized page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ff5b416bccf6e4588c36c1fb30708229552c717","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/7ff5b416bccf6e4588c36c1fb30708229552c717"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDlmNDViOTZlMTFmNDM0YWFkNTc5OGY5NTkzMzk2YTFjZTliMTljMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e","sha":"93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e"}],"sha":"9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/9f45b96e11f434aad5798f9593396a1ce9b19c2c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:56:39Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:48:42Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix: backfill a changed template with one flow per page of nodes\n\nA display label, HFID or Jinja2 computed attribute template change backfills\nevery node of the kind. The trigger flow submitted one process flow per node,\nawaiting each submission, so a kind with 151k nodes took about 9 hours at\n~4.5 submissions/s, even when every value was already current (as after a\nmerge that carried the recomputed values: every flow was a no-op).\n\nSubmit one process flow per page of node ids instead, sized by the\nsubmission chunk, through the coalesced `object_ids` path the merge and\nrebase recompute already use. A rebase replaying the same 157k interfaces\nthrough that path finished in 108 s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fab782a94f79b37a4b05626e7de2fe85d9b911f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/5fab782a94f79b37a4b05626e7de2fe85d9b911f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDkzZTE3MDM5Zjc2MzFhODhmOGQ4MmZiZDI5MmJkNjhhNmRlZjQ1MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c","sha":"8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c"}],"sha":"93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/93e17039f7631a88f8d82fbd292bd68a6def452e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40861490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/polmichel","id":40861490,"login":"polmichel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODYxNDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:44:29Z","email":"40861490+polmichel@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pol Michel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:44:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(frontend): keep the retry notice up until the latest grace has passed (#10761)\n\nEach replay that fired started its own grace timer, so when two replays\nsettled within the grace period the first timer closed the shared notice\nbefore the second one''s grace ended, and a replay shed again in that\nwindow reopened the notice instead of updating it. One cancellable timer\nnow follows the latest settlement.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24891e0c7dd870d8490d8e9d0fd990bd259cd728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/24891e0c7dd870d8490d8e9d0fd990bd259cd728"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c","verification":{"payload":"tree 24891e0c7dd870d8490d8e9d0fd990bd259cd728\nparent 08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca\nauthor Pol Michel <40861490+polmichel@users.noreply.github.com> 1790775869 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790775869 +0200\n\nfix(frontend): keep the retry notice up until the latest grace has passed (#10761)\n\nEach replay that fired started its own grace timer, so when two replays\nsettled within the grace period the first timer closed the shared notice\nbefore the second one''s grace ended, and a replay shed again in that\nwindow reopened the notice instead of updating it. One cancellable timer\nnow follows the latest settlement.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRI9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+NkQALIaPlcVrQHPe/Fmik9HiSyD\nsaauGhOJkuCc70IaySwuShR/D6Os212X7fEzOGhbRmFcFvDIgvZBdyhdUDORYJiJ\ncLtcqx/ZFFHGneQ+v0xyuLlTpkBfpujvQ1IJ+1B8PgoNFVxXzHGiWM/B2mvGyCZ1\n1uy5enxIpuo1hpAE0YCphtDmzMxGqDrKq+jpeEh312vDJ45q1qPLdeiZiI2NvF3U\nuVfXgKrT0rX4qDPf91c8TQXcypuGn6evRO+uY5M3q5dzIJh0KUjArT8u43mkBqQn\nLF8gDWENPZ91sTtDK5Mv0VFRea4wd7aDVa20NTtZMTqHtOTueTFXDabMIiRQxYtZ\nAjrqW6KS8QewH8VOibliSpYcOuPPdEbHz+PgIYxls2Lx3nzZEhRnUjBfU8bfBCs7\nMgpZJRAkKH3viXgyqq2nioXoQ4cBPQMeyf10N9bNq9X5Iijtb4zuw6KNwpl12Q3o\nudUo9sOj9snXfzIpg8taJSBLGcflWiPFuhpcbTHSrDFCnLSbAC4ehlAF0sb/dSLq\nVKTeHUPrp+oevWnvYwNawfICB8IkrAk2LpAbvqks8qLmtu7RFaHzFFczNEYnLE5j\nwuVd1NxeCaTq29R5/2s8VvfHlcd8B8+Ow7gQZOyDDcPzu5XH9mAWWdcY4U3hEg9D\nzDKW1RG3B+Qk7jLoTL8n\n=pOag\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:44:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDhmMDU2YTkzZWU3Zjk0NGFkNDY1MTk4M2QxM2RkYTE2NjM1YTQ4NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca","sha":"08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca"}],"sha":"8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8f056a93ee7f944ad4651983d13dda16635a485c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:09:40Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(branch): keep refusing a rebase through a relationship property conflict\n\nA rebase keeps the branch''s edges, but a relationship property edge hangs from\na relationship vertex the default branch can disconnect. On the car/person\nfixtures, with the branch setting is_protected on a car''s driver and the\nconflicts resolved for the branch:\n- the default branch clearing the driver left the rebased branch with no\n  driver at all;\n- the default branch re-pointing the driver, whose only conflict is on the old\n  peer''s side, left the branch with the new driver and without its change.\nBefore the rebase accepted resolved conflicts it refused both, as stable does.\n\nA rebase now lets through only attribute conflicts resolved for the branch, and\nnot one whose default branch side is REMOVED, as for an attribute the default\nbranch removed. Every relationship conflict needs a data update again. The\nproposed change view offers the branch choice only for attribute values anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60f0b21ff830f082f6a575d37792b79847cd7342","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/60f0b21ff830f082f6a575d37792b79847cd7342"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDA4YmNjYjcxYmY4MDYxM2YzZDI3NWZjODYyOTg0NjZjYjJhMGEzY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb","sha":"7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb"}],"sha":"08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/08bccb71bf80613f3d275fc86298466cb2a0a3ca"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:09:31Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"test: serve component tests one shared in-memory cache\n\nThe rebase tests overrode build_cache with `lambda: MemoryCache()`, which hands\nevery get_cache() call a new, empty cache, while production resolves one\nsingleton: a value one caller writes, such as the merge write block, would be\ninvisible to the next. The fixture now closes over a single MemoryCache and\nlives in the component conftest next to workflow_recorder, so other component\ntests that run a flow can reuse it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"913fd0c2e6c21d37bd74f65171ffc9d8a3a2a767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/913fd0c2e6c21d37bd74f65171ffc9d8a3a2a767"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDdhZjQ0Y2FkM2E4YzQ5ODcxNTNmZTUwMmEyMzAxNzNkYjc5NmE4Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa","sha":"9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa"}],"sha":"7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7af44cad3a8c4987153fe502a230173db796a8cb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:54:09Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs(diff): say why a recalculation reads only the partner diff''s metadata\n\nNow that a branch''s default branch diff is scoped to the branch''s nodes, it\noutgrows the branch side only for a diff stored by an earlier version; the\nreason to skip its nodes is that a recalculation replaces it and reads only its\nuuid and proposed change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e89299d44c6983fc083d10d956155ff194f44ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/0e89299d44c6983fc083d10d956155ff194f44ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDllYmVjMTQzMzgyOTcwNmEwNWIyOWVmNGI4MTFkMTc5ODk1MjkyZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed","sha":"20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed"}],"sha":"9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/9ebec1433829706a05b29ef4b811d179895292fa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:54:09Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(branch): tell the user what each conflict blocking a rebase needs\n\nThe rebase error described what a rebase does with a conflict rather than what\nto do about it, and did not say where a conflict gets resolved. It now splits\nthe blocking conflicts in two:\n- attribute and relationship property conflicts that are unresolved or\n  resolved for the default branch: resolve them in favor of the branch, in a\n  proposed change or with the ResolveDiffConflict mutation, or update the data;\n- node and cardinality-one peer conflicts: update the data so both branches\n  agree.\n\nThe proposed change view only offers the branch choice for an attribute value,\nso the docs point at ResolveDiffConflict and the DiffTree conflict ID for the\nother properties. A NEED_UPGRADE_REBASE branch accepts both: only NEED_REBASE\nis gated by the mutation middleware.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3efc76ef957969f81ddf698357c4ae811cac107a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/3efc76ef957969f81ddf698357c4ae811cac107a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDIwZjJhNzZlZDE5NTg2Zjk1OGNiYmQzZDE3N2Y5NjBlOGRhNDE0ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525","sha":"c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525"}],"sha":"20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/20f2a76ed19586f958cbbd3d177f960e8da414ed"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:16:53Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"test(branch): serve the rebase flow''s cache from memory in the rebase tests\n\nThe rebase flow reads the merge write block from the cache, and the tests that\nrun it built the real cache. They only passed when an earlier module on the\nsame xdist worker had started an app through TestInfrahubApp: its client\nfixture points the settings at the session Redis container and leaves a\nworking cache singleton behind. On #10765 core/test_get_kinds_lock.py and\nproposed_change/test_request_generator_definition_check.py ran on gw0 before\nthis module; the added cases shifted the schedule, neither ran first, and\ntest_rebase_schemas_handed_to_the_update_coordinator and\ntest_failed_rebase_keeps_the_branch_data hit localhost:6379 and failed.\n\nA memory_cache fixture now overrides build_cache for every test here that runs\nthe flow. The module passes on its own without Redis (10 passed; both tests\nfailed before).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fe4b4b15061d3199e42749879f06d278888e087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/2fe4b4b15061d3199e42749879f06d278888e087"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGMwNGJmY2M2NWYyMGRkZWJhNTJkNzkwYmE1NTFiMzVkY2MzNGY1MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183","sha":"b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183"}],"sha":"c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c04bfcc65f20ddeba52d790ba551b35dcc34f525"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:59:31Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(branch): let a rebase through conflicts resolved in favor of the branch\n\nA branch in NEED_UPGRADE_REBASE with conflicts had no way out: BranchMerge and\na proposed change merge refuse that status, and the rebase refused every\nconflict whatever its selected_branch, so the only escape was editing the\ndefault branch to match the branch (the routing-policy branch''s four\nCoreGeneratorDefinition fingerprint conflicts).\n\nA rebase keeps the branch''s edge for every conflicting field, so it already\nproduces the branch-side resolution for attribute and relationship property\nconflicts. It now lets those through once they are resolved in favor of the\nbranch. It still refuses:\n- unresolved conflicts and ones resolved in favor of the default branch,\n  which a rebase cannot apply;\n- node-level conflicts, which are never resolvable;\n- cardinality-one peer conflicts: probed on a car whose owner changed on\n  both sides, the rebased branch reads two owners (\"Too many relationships,\n  max 1 at owner\"), since the default branch''s new relationship stays\n  visible next to the branch''s.\n\nThe all-conflicts query now returns the level each conflict is attached to.\nThe error lists the blocking conflict paths. The rejection cases fail against\nthe old gate (message) and the cardinality-one case fails without the level\ncheck; the success case fails against the old gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f91dee83e44cb4ce48389ff0474e529d01fd15e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/6f91dee83e44cb4ce48389ff0474e529d01fd15e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGI2NDQxMjcyMTRhOTEzMGMxYjIwNmRlYjYyODIzZjdjM2RkMmExODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d","sha":"b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d"}],"sha":"b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/b644127214a9130c1b206deb62823f7c3dd2a183"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:34:06Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): read only the metadata of the partner diff when recreating a diff\n\nA diff refresh loaded the default branch side of the previous diff in full,\nalthough it only reads that root''s uuid and proposed change. A diff stored\nbefore the base-side scoping fix can hold every change the default branch\nmade since the branch was created: on the bench-customer backup the old base\ndiff had 383k nodes, the refresh tracked 78-106M objects with 18-30 s GC\npauses, let its heartbeat key expire and held the diff lock a following\nmerge was waiting on.\n\nThe partner root is now read through the roots metadata query, which takes a\ndiff_ids filter, so a refresh loads only the branch side. The component test\nfails when the old call is restored: the recording repository then also sees\n(''main'', <partner uuid>).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50f93791971fcc23d662c8731a153090b141b4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/50f93791971fcc23d662c8731a153090b141b4a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGI0ZmFlYmEzODZhZTFiMmQyYWViNWM4NzQzMzcxYTJiZTIyNWYwN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c","sha":"a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c"}],"sha":"b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/b4faeba386ae1b2d2aeb5c8743371a2be225f07d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:17:51Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs(branch): say every rebase replays all of the branch''s own changes\n\nA rebase moves every change on the branch to the rebase time, so each\nrebase replays all of them again, where a merge replays them once. The\nchangelog and the knowledge page said \"as a merge does\", and the rebase\norigin row left out the default branch''s changes replayed for the kinds\nwhose schema the branch changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2a55257af613f6eca4d6256ae450e0d6da4a525","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/c2a55257af613f6eca4d6256ae450e0d6da4a525"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGE1NjkwYTg5NTQ2N2JmOTdiOWI1MTI5ZDgzMzUzYWZhZDBjYjU3MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac","sha":"647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac"}],"sha":"a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a5690a895467bf97b9b5129d83353afad0cb571c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:17:51Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs(diff): scope the changed-node listing docstring to the requested kinds\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8267e16b373a478a1bcfbc111ba765b8c23ee013","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/8267e16b373a478a1bcfbc111ba765b8c23ee013"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDY0NzE4MWFjMjc1ZmVmNjZhOTk1NDEyOTdkNDc5ZDRlYTA3YmRiYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f","sha":"4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f"}],"sha":"647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/647181ac275fef66a99541297d479d4ea07bdbac"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:17:51Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"test(diff): cover the kind-migrated node listing across pages and kinds\n\nThe listing of the nodes a kind migration touched pages by uuid. A page\nwhose rows the diff already held, or whose rows the requested node\nkinds leave out, now keeps the listing going, and the rows of other\nkinds are left out of the diff. The test pages two rows at a time over\nthree migrated cars, the two on the first page already in the diff.\n\nIt fails for new_kind_only when the paging reads has_more_data only\nfrom a row that added a node, and for new_kind_only and unrelated_kind\nwithout the node kinds filter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7d94f965f41ca593fedb933f83e4241a8e80d19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/c7d94f965f41ca593fedb933f83e4241a8e80d19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDRiZjg4NmI5ZDdmNzk0OTllYzYxNmQzY2Y0Y2YzN2U5MDI4ZmM5MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4","sha":"e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4"}],"sha":"4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/4bf886b9d7f79499ec616d3cf4cf37e9028fc92f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:52:13Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs(branch): reword the rebase replay comments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48adb454e59e9cbcfa81cf1d300267136bcb738c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/48adb454e59e9cbcfa81cf1d300267136bcb738c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGUwNjQyOTFmZGFmODUwZjQ1YmQzNzRjZWRjNGNlMGU1OGRkZmQ1ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341","sha":"698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341"}],"sha":"e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/e064291fdaf850f45bd374cedc4ce0e58ddfd5e4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:52:13Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(merge): recompute all of a rebased node''s own derived values\n\nA rebase replays the branch''s own changes, and an updated node\nrecomputed only its own derived values that read a changed field. A\nvalue that reads no changed field kept what it derived from the old\nbase. A computed attribute a schema change adds on the branch is written\non every node of its kind, so the node''s only changed field is the\ncomputed attribute itself: when the default branch renamed the peers it\nreads, nothing refreshed it after the rebase.\n\nWith the replay flag, an updated node now recomputes all of its own\nderived values, while its cross-node readers keep the field filter.\nDisplay labels and human-friendly ids already refreshed the node\nwhatever the changed fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"162f1718fb5fea76a7790c325ce517bb78609521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/162f1718fb5fea76a7790c325ce517bb78609521"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDY5OGM3MTE2MmM5MTcxMjBiMjNhNjYyMmI3YzNjZjg5NGIwMjczNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412","sha":"348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412"}],"sha":"698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/698c71162c917120b23a6622b7c3cf894b027341"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:35:35Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(changelog): keep the changelog of a relationship a schema migration removed\n\nThe changelog of a relationship looks its peer''s kind up in the diff,\nthen in the schema. When a schema migration removed the relationship or\nits node''s kind, the schema lookup raised, and the whole changelog\ncollection failed with it.\n\nA rebase that replays the branch''s own changes hits this when the\ndefault branch removed a relationship the branch changed: the rebased\nschema no longer has it, and the unchanged peer is not in the branch''s\ndiff. The peer kind is now reported as \"n/a\", as an attribute''s kind\nalready is when a migration removed the attribute.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23d56463b317dcdcbfd3d624091367faa7f81544","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/23d56463b317dcdcbfd3d624091367faa7f81544"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDM0OGRlNzFjODRlNzRiYzQxZjU1NWFjMzdlNzFjM2Q4NWY0OWE0MTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494","sha":"8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494"}],"sha":"348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/348de71c84e74bc41f555ac37e71c3d85f49a412"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:26:15Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(branch): replay a rebased branch''s own changes instead of the default branch''s\n\nA rebase replayed every change made on the default branch since the fork\nonto the branch, as node events and a coalesced recompute. Its cost\nfollowed the default branch''s activity: a bulk import there made the\nrebase of any branch with changes of its own calculate a diff of every\nimported object, and it fired webhooks, action rules and Python-transform\nrecomputes on the branch for each of them.\n\nA rebase now replays onto the new base what a merge replays onto the\ndestination, the branch''s own changes, read from the branch''s diff:\n\n- one rebase node event per node in the branch''s diff;\n- the coalesced recompute built from those changes, with the builder''s\n  new refresh_updated_nodes, since the values an updated node refreshed\n  inline on its save read the old base;\n- a profile refresh for every node whose profiles changed on the branch.\n\nA value on the branch that never depended on the branch''s changes\nalready reads what the default branch computed, except where the branch\nchanged the schema: the default branch derived its values with its own\nschema. The default branch''s changes are therefore still replayed for\nthe kinds whose schema on the rebased branch differs from the default\nbranch''s (SchemaBranch.get_object_kinds_different_from), through the\nkind-scoped unstored diff.\n\nMeasured on a copy of a customer database, for the branch\nfeature/routing-policy-relationships (3,195 nodes in its diff, schema\nchanges on 12 kinds): its own diff loads in under a second, and the\ndefault-branch diff scoped to the kinds it changed holds 2,433 nodes,\ncalculated in 122 s at under 1 GB of worker memory. The replay of every\ndefault-branch change it replaced covers 382,705 nodes, about 27 minutes\nof calculation and more than 30 GB of worker memory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fcd805741b76866ba1d9cd06528c0148e3d42928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/fcd805741b76866ba1d9cd06528c0148e3d42928"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDgyMjI5MDYxMzkzMTlmNmEyZDFlODQ0NTQ0OTQ2ZjJlNjI4MGE0OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f","sha":"8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f"}],"sha":"8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8222906139319f6a2d1e844544946f2e6280a494"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:26:15Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:37:05Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): let a diff calculation cover chosen node kinds only\n\nThe changed-node listings that drive each level of a diff calculation\ntake an optional list of node kinds, and DiffCalculator.calculate_diff\nand DiffCoordinator.calculate_arbitrary_timeframe_diff pass it through.\nThe paths queries already run per chunk of the listed nodes, so the\ncalculation only reads the nodes of those kinds.\n\nThe nodes added for a kind migration are filtered the same way. Their\npagination now reads has_more_data from every row of a page: it used to\nread it only from a row that added a new node, so a page whose rows were\nall known nodes ended the pagination early.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"12a7bad9a7fefad428013776a796eb8b4c016618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/12a7bad9a7fefad428013776a796eb8b4c016618"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDgzMDRiNTUxZTU1NGQ5ZDU2MTdkOThmOTBlZGYzZjE4OTEzY2I0M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e","sha":"034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e"}],"sha":"8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8304b551e554d9d5617d98f90edf3f18913cb43f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:00:55Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:28:24Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(cli): wait for merges and keep merged branches'' diffs in delete-diffs\n\nA merge refreshes its branch diff, then reads and freezes it outside the\ndiff update locks, holding only the global merge lock for the whole\nflow. Deleting a branch diff in one of those gaps either lets the merge\nrun without its conflict resolutions before rolling it back, or loses\nthe diff the merged branch was about to freeze. The deleter now takes\nthe global merge lock, before the diff update locks as the merge does,\nfor every batch that holds a branch diff. Named diffs are not read by\nmerges, so deleting them does not wait for one.\n\nA merge tolerates failing to freeze its branch diff, and a merged\nbranch''s diff cannot be calculated again. --include-branch-diffs now\nkeeps the unfrozen branch diffs of merged branches and reports them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"21820e0256fbcf1bf5daca52691a089fbccdff04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/21820e0256fbcf1bf5daca52691a089fbccdff04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDAzNDk0MmM4NjJhZTk5NzIyNWE1OTY2NDY0NWFjZTk1YzZjNmMxNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2","sha":"7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2"}],"sha":"034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/034942c862ae997225a59664645ace95c6c6c15e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:58:05Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:28:24Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"feat(cli): delete only named diffs unless --include-branch-diffs is given\n\n`infrahub db delete-diffs` now deletes the unfrozen named diffs by\ndefault. Named diffs are cheap to lose: besides the ones requested\nthrough the API, merges and rebases each save a uniquely named diff of\nthe default branch that is never read again. Branch-tracking diffs are\nonly deleted with --include-branch-diffs, since each one has to be\ncalculated again in full and loses its recorded conflict resolutions.\n\n--branch now accepts the default branch, which is where those merge and\nrebase leftovers live, along with base roots left without their branch\nroot.\n\nPlanning and deletion are split into UnfrozenDiffDeletionPlanner and\nUnfrozenDiffDeleter, and the deleter takes the whole plan, deleting it\nbranch by branch under each branch''s diff update locks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"49625fc45f3f3bbf0bb8def643235bd9e33e824d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/49625fc45f3f3bbf0bb8def643235bd9e33e824d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDc3NDBhMGVhMDQwYmNmMWJiMzk0NDg5YmU2NmY0MWYwMGE1NGQ3YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3","sha":"a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3"}],"sha":"7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7740a0ea040bcf1bb394489be66f41f00a54d7a2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:27:46Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:28:24Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"feat(cli): add a command to delete the diffs that are not frozen\n\n`infrahub db delete-diffs` deletes every stored diff that is not frozen,\nor only those of the branch given with --branch, which may already be\ndeleted. Frozen diffs, the record kept for closed or merged proposed\nchanges and for merged or deleted branches, are left alone.\n\nA diff is stored as a branch root paired with a base root, and the delete\nquery follows the partner edge from the base root into the branch root:\ndeleting a base root alone removes the whole pair. The command therefore\ndeletes pairs, and skips a pair outright when either root is frozen, so\nan unfrozen root never takes a frozen partner down with it.\n\nEach branch''s diffs are deleted under the incremental and full diff\nupdate locks of that branch, so an update in progress finishes first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3bb592698be3d1ed46feb6bd40886f1a58e88ad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/3bb592698be3d1ed46feb6bd40886f1a58e88ad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGE3ZTgzOTBjMzVkMjAyMGYwY2YxMWM1ZDRhZWJlMjNkNWMzM2E5ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59","sha":"950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59"}],"sha":"a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/a7e8390c35d2020f0cf11c5d4aebe23d5c33a9d3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:13:37Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:47:54Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(branch): stop storing a rebase''s default-branch diff, skip it when unused\n\nAfter the graph rebase, the rebase calculated a diff of every change on\nthe default branch between the old branched_from and the rebase time and\nstored it under a random name nothing reads back, only to turn it into\nrebase node events and the coalesced recompute. Its cost follows the\ndefault branch''s activity since the fork, not the branch: a bulk import\non the default branch made it take tens of minutes and tens of GB of\nworker memory, and every rebase left an orphaned diff root behind.\n\n- The diff is calculated and enriched in memory by a new\n  DiffCoordinator.calculate_arbitrary_timeframe_diff, without the diff\n  lock or a save.\n- It is skipped when the branch''s own diff holds no node: such a branch\n  reads what the default branch holds once rebased, so there is nothing\n  to replay onto it; it gets the BranchRebasedEvent alone.\n- It is skipped when events are not sent, since only the events and the\n  recompute read it; the upgrade command rebases branches that way.\n\nOn a copy of the customer database the branch that triggered this has\nno node in its diff, so its rebase no longer calculates the 382k-node\ndefault-branch diff at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9bdc17cd5c9d6b5f0a55618f34364cc31cd2f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/a9bdc17cd5c9d6b5f0a55618f34364cc31cd2f88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDk1MGYzOTJjMTc5OTRjN2ViZGIyMTEwYzMzODczY2VmYTMxNWFmNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c","sha":"23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c"}],"sha":"950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/950f392c17994c7ebdb2110c33873cefa315af59"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:13:37Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:47:54Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): enrich and save a diff of a branch against itself once\n\nA diff of a branch against itself is calculated as one root that stands\nfor both sides of the pair, but it was turned into two enriched copies\nsharing one uuid: every enricher ran on both, the conflicts enricher\ncompared each node with itself, and the save wrote every node twice into\nthe same diff root.\n\nThe pair now holds one enriched root for both sides, the enrichers and\nthe save iterate its distinct roots, and the conflicts enricher returns\nearly for a root compared with itself. The stored shape is unchanged:\none diff root, as before.\n\nMeasured on a 13k-node sample of a customer''s default-branch diff\n(382k nodes in full): enrichment halves, and the save takes 0.56x the\ntime of writing both copies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9364c8ed524a08ddb4aca07fd89706d95270dcdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/9364c8ed524a08ddb4aca07fd89706d95270dcdf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDIzZjcxOTEwNzBmZTQwOGQwN2MwOWZlZTg4Yjg3Zjk0NWVmZTQxMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53","sha":"c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53"}],"sha":"23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/23f7191070fe408d07c09fee88b87f945efe410c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40861490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/polmichel","id":40861490,"login":"polmichel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODYxNDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T21:43:36Z","email":"40861490+polmichel@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pol Michel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T21:43:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: address the low-cost Cubic hygiene findings from #10693 (#10758)\n\n* test: skip the diff index migration test outside Neo4j\n\nThe migration only manages Neo4j indexes and returns early elsewhere, so\nits pre-state assertion cannot hold on another database.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: keep the branch refresh schedule out of the heartbeat gating test\n\nThe scheduler still creates the branch refresh task when it is not\nrunning, and with a zero start delay that task reaches the service check\nand raises in the background.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: quote the expected CA bundle path the way urlencode does\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: cancel the NATS initialisation task when the wait for connect fails\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(frontend): drop the stale Content-Length from a reworded shed response\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cc3967d2a37601f1e2b74f9c29eb49548fa098e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/0cc3967d2a37601f1e2b74f9c29eb49548fa098e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53","verification":{"payload":"tree 0cc3967d2a37601f1e2b74f9c29eb49548fa098e\nparent 8ebc36f5f074195346f28eb96e62129325780e45\nauthor Pol Michel <40861490+polmichel@users.noreply.github.com> 1790718216 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790718216 +0200\n\ntest: address the low-cost Cubic hygiene findings from #10693 (#10758)\n\n* test: skip the diff index migration test outside Neo4j\n\nThe migration only manages Neo4j indexes and returns early elsewhere, so\nits pre-state assertion cannot hold on another database.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: keep the branch refresh schedule out of the heartbeat gating test\n\nThe scheduler still creates the branch refresh task when it is not\nrunning, and with a zero start delay that task reaches the service check\nand raises in the background.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: quote the expected CA bundle path the way urlencode does\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: cancel the NATS initialisation task when the wait for connect fails\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(frontend): drop the stale Content-Length from a reworded shed response\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvDEICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm4IQAEuCiMaRJPokz6cwV/0XKbX8\ndEKwd5xAcowodFbfT8zCM6zZO7rH7ZmOjb5q5dz8VWbv4xAUmOhn3+nD5TC+SvSW\nt/1Jc0hfAbJxkcFOjg8W33jHVo1QsdEGYJwEmK2qRMGSvo3TGTcdxbd1gkJW34ja\nhK8DdfxLQjlRQOmuCqaewrARbwcQfrpg9kz4bH4RZ2Nw0TJJqRyamlNRASd5cGy5\nWIveNhoU4nHFyknIdi91+l1XY0poKkMeo8nxxjlEcvYczcV/qLCQgmXcyB4Q1TyM\nIb8RbEDE3YIHOjgsIE2DguawcDCoF9wBiNxjZQzptOkTIqdpdPDwoIzi7gdI/+h5\n+7RhHcnL8EirfkxfvVGN+10gkpPSPczhykSat77KQcgUqOOsgOQxU+OsjXMNIJ8w\njPKstmLe0bRIPoBpfYtYjcgPBZXCwfl7ZGDUX5zLbjMcXLHM5a+zR+j/3YZP8JRO\nJbVOurwpg4dDK+g0sBj4ZwBNfT0+mLjSo3wp+6b1DY2fqOJz/yC/J/icopZAOfMZ\n8AGqrTdsmGulf3XR4ruvEivRDS8GaBIuAYhAatf4dhS7imMjxkQXfEBSxR4Urj32\nTJeBRuzEtbYeaFmbRvDcV2HgkcM9jJkKzw0hvBo2nRiKlGO4j2anPGxXIwLjGW2s\nI+7DODcRdd5b5bkQwkKv\n=aEab\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T21:43:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGM0OWU1YTQ0YjNlODA2ZDYyYTc0ZmJhNzNiMzE1Mjk1ODliOGNlNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/8ebc36f5f074195346f28eb96e62129325780e45","sha":"8ebc36f5f074195346f28eb96e62129325780e45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8ebc36f5f074195346f28eb96e62129325780e45"}],"sha":"c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c49e5a44b3e806d62a74fba73b31529589b8ce53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40861490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/polmichel","id":40861490,"login":"polmichel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODYxNDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/polmichel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/8ebc36f5f074195346f28eb96e62129325780e45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T21:42:54Z","email":"40861490+polmichel@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Pol Michel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T21:42:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: address the Cubic documentation-accuracy findings from #10693 (#10702)\n\n* docs: state the real batch fan-out in the agnostic retirement query\n\nThe batch memory bound omitted the field and peer expansion that happens\nbefore the rows are multiplied by the branch count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: describe duplicate preservation under UNION ALL in the retirement query\n\nThe comment credited UNION ALL with an aggregation it does not perform;\nnodes matching both candidate bounds survive twice and are evaluated twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: describe how Prefect trims an event''s run-context resources\n\nThe knowledge page said the events worker extends the related list past\nthe maximum and that the API closes the event stream. Prefect 3.8.6\nattaches only as many run-context resources as still fit under the\nmaximum and logs a warning for the rest, so an event emitted on the\nmaximum reaches the API valid but without its run context. The\ndocstrings in events/limits.py already describe this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: read the configured gitconfig path in the private CA verification step\n\nThe prose already said the path is named by INFRAHUB_GIT_GLOBAL_CONFIG_FILE,\nbut the command hard-coded the default, so a deployment that moves the file\ngets a false negative.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: note that the worker gitconfig path is operator-configurable\n\nTwo bullets pinned the file to /opt/infrahub/.gitconfig, which is only the\ndefault of git.global_config_file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: name the exception branch creation actually raises\n\nThe docstring example documented BranchExistsError, which does not exist;\na duplicate branch name raises ValidationError.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop the restating field docstrings from RelationshipPeerData\n\nThe guidelines label this exact pattern as bad while the class shipped it,\nincluding a properties docstring that described a different field. The one\ndocstring that carries information is kept.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: state the heartbeat refresh interval as 5 s in the merge recovery spec\n\nHEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SECONDS is 5.0 against a 15 s TTL, so the key is written\nthree times per expiry. Both files carrying the inherited 10 s figure are\nupdated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: qualify how the offline validator''s loc compares to the server''s\n\nvalidate_schema() runs on the schema dict alone, so its loc starts at the\nschema root and omits the request-envelope prefix the 422 detail carries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e49ad229139f59d1e29918fb7cac68c545e035f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/5e49ad229139f59d1e29918fb7cac68c545e035f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/8ebc36f5f074195346f28eb96e62129325780e45","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e49ad229139f59d1e29918fb7cac68c545e035f\nparent 304579e2608973f17ac4246aed637eee6a6f4386\nauthor Pol Michel <40861490+polmichel@users.noreply.github.com> 1790718174 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790718174 +0200\n\ndocs: address the Cubic documentation-accuracy findings from #10693 (#10702)\n\n* docs: state the real batch fan-out in the agnostic retirement query\n\nThe batch memory bound omitted the field and peer expansion that happens\nbefore the rows are multiplied by the branch count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: describe duplicate preservation under UNION ALL in the retirement query\n\nThe comment credited UNION ALL with an aggregation it does not perform;\nnodes matching both candidate bounds survive twice and are evaluated twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: describe how Prefect trims an event''s run-context resources\n\nThe knowledge page said the events worker extends the related list past\nthe maximum and that the API closes the event stream. Prefect 3.8.6\nattaches only as many run-context resources as still fit under the\nmaximum and logs a warning for the rest, so an event emitted on the\nmaximum reaches the API valid but without its run context. The\ndocstrings in events/limits.py already describe this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: read the configured gitconfig path in the private CA verification step\n\nThe prose already said the path is named by INFRAHUB_GIT_GLOBAL_CONFIG_FILE,\nbut the command hard-coded the default, so a deployment that moves the file\ngets a false negative.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: note that the worker gitconfig path is operator-configurable\n\nTwo bullets pinned the file to /opt/infrahub/.gitconfig, which is only the\ndefault of git.global_config_file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: name the exception branch creation actually raises\n\nThe docstring example documented BranchExistsError, which does not exist;\na duplicate branch name raises ValidationError.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop the restating field docstrings from RelationshipPeerData\n\nThe guidelines label this exact pattern as bad while the class shipped it,\nincluding a properties docstring that described a different field. The one\ndocstring that carries information is kept.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: state the heartbeat refresh interval as 5 s in the merge recovery spec\n\nHEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SECONDS is 5.0 against a 15 s TTL, so the key is written\nthree times per expiry. Both files carrying the inherited 10 s figure are\nupdated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: qualify how the offline validator''s loc compares to the server''s\n\nvalidate_schema() runs on the schema dict alone, so its loc starts at the\nschema root and omits the request-envelope prefix the 422 detail carries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvDDeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2+YQAHBcbtcEuH38xmxDgepjv1xI\nIG65HAphAH1TMIUtc+NXwPEG9v1JP5DPS80ROco+2dSidFOGy/HPnbLfaVn1Zurs\nmdsl1Bvtry1SeBYCkfNL5pfYzWahZ2IfayNjfxcef86m7zWoSZ7vOpg/ilRlhuMd\nZkmfk0CK1eao2diYpS5QLDZambp06BarFnM5xnloNvNNfccdw9o2MoklHYE2XKkx\nL7FT2Ae0MOQ1XvKi2u8+MyyZ1itnVrfKkkVo60Ahf4+1Xm6JOypBbYILsjlkhWLH\n+s+qVvgUraWNgwgnWCNJhtIjQDzFbuXi6rIyUkCyeUToONo2oasOHqgaaTByC//5\nsm3/jZZ7CcFTVietyoHhldcsniYOqp0n3UwE1e+fAEpS2JOacI8InbNd1OTGRfIm\nUHFEvnGdyjaLRSOx9rdb3038YZ