url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/11402e9b4caf895f852323c5ba206d8ae85ffb24","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDExNDAyZTliNGNhZjg5NWY4NTIzMjNjNWJhMjA2ZDhhZTg1ZmZiMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e","sha":"e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e"}],"sha":"11402e9b4caf895f852323c5ba206d8ae85ffb24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/11402e9b4caf895f852323c5ba206d8ae85ffb24"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:33:12Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:55:44Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"feat(config): add tls_insecure to S3 storage and log-forwarding destinations\n\nS3 object storage and syslog destinations were the only outbound TLS\ncomponents without a way to skip certificate validation, although the\nprivate CA guide promises a *_TLS_INSECURE setting for each of them.\n\n- storage.s3.tls_insecure (INFRAHUB_STORAGE_TLS_INSECURE) passes\n  verify=False to boto3. It outranks tls_ca_file, like git, HTTP, the\n  database, the broker and the cache, and is rejected with\n  use_ssl=false, like tls_ca_file already is. Both compose files\n  forward it.\n- Log-forwarding destinations gain tls_insecure\n  (INFRAHUB_LOG_FORWARDING_DESTINATION_<NAME>_TLS_INSECURE), rejected\n  without tls_enabled so a plaintext destination never silently ignores\n  it. This repo only defines the setting; the Enterprise TCP transport\n  applies it.\n\nThe global tls.ca_bundle already skips insecure components, so both\nare left alone once the flag is set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bcb3f2a46414aa768d0909e26b28d5a24d18e02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/9bcb3f2a46414aa768d0909e26b28d5a24d18e02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGUyMzAzNGU5MjkxZGYxYTJiOTYyYjE0Yzk5ZDYzOTg3NGNkZjkzMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988","sha":"165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988"}],"sha":"e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/e23034e9291df1a2b962b14c99d639874cdf932e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:02:41Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:55:13Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): ignore base-branch paths added and removed before an incremental window\n\nA path whose edge was added and then closed within the diff''s timeframe\nleaves no net change and is skipped. The parser judged that against the\nstart of the current window, but the base-branch history of a field the\nbranch changes for the first time is read from the fork point. A peer\nthe base branch added and removed between the fork and the window was\ntherefore kept, and showed up as added in the base diff.\n\nJudge it against the fork point for those paths, the same start the\nfield query already uses for them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6415e0967aaaff587c8cec445102520aafae0f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/e6415e0967aaaff587c8cec445102520aafae0f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDE2NWQ3Njc1NzY4OTEyZDc4NDJkYmM1YTFmNzc2NmU4ZDZiMDQ5ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82","sha":"7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82"}],"sha":"165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/165d7675768912d7842dbc5a1f7766e8d6b04988"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:54:30Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:55:13Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): capture base-branch relationship removals before an incremental window\n\nAn incremental diff reads the base-branch history of a field back to\nthe fork point once the branch changes that field for the first time.\nFor a relationship, a removal on the branch that owns the edge only\nsets `to` on the active edge, and the parser turned that into a delete\nonly when `to` fell after the start of the current window. A removal\nmade before the window was dropped, so its conflict was never reported.\n\nThe base diff of a branch with no diffed changes used to be unscoped\nand store the removal early, which hid this for that case; scoping it\nmade TestDiffUpdateConflict fail. For a branch that already had changes,\nthe base diff missed the removal on stable too.\n\nJudge the delete against the relationship''s own start, which is the\nfork point for a field new to the branch and the window start otherwise.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19df4e704b065f3892397abc152a4595ea5436f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/19df4e704b065f3892397abc152a4595ea5436f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDc2NTNjZDY1NjRkMzI0ZTVkMWNiZGVhOWMwNmEwZjUxYTZkMDdlODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03","sha":"3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03"}],"sha":"7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7653cd6564d324e5d1cbdea9c06a0f51a6d07e82"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:22:47Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:55:13Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"chore(review): address review nitpicks\n\nDescribe the rebase and branch-delete candidate windows separately in\nthe branch-agnostic retirement notes, and share the retirement query\ntests'' class-scoped fixtures at module level.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7da73503650f6eeeafbf958251da962add5f152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/c7da73503650f6eeeafbf958251da962add5f152"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDNlOWFjMGE0ODY5N2QzZDI0NjRmNTk3Mjc1NTU4ODI2YzJhZGJlMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e","sha":"c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e"}],"sha":"3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:40:47Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:55:13Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(branch): read the default-branch deletions a rebase absorbs from the graph\n\nThe rebase re-evaluates the branch-agnostic fields of the nodes deleted\non the default branch within the window it closes. It read those nodes\nfrom the stored base-branch diff, which is scoped to the fields the\nbranch changed: it lists a default-branch deletion only when the branch\nchanged that node too. A branch with changes of its own therefore\nreleased none of the deletions it rebased past, and a branch without\nany only did because its base diff was unscoped, which the previous\ncommit fixes.\n\nQuery the nodes whose default-branch existence edge turned deleted\nbetween the branch''s previous fork point and the rebase timestamp,\nboth included, as branch deletion already does from its fork point.\nThe uuids come back in one row: IS_PART_OF is indexed on the branch\nonly, and a paged read would rescan the default branch''s existence\nedges once per page while the global graph lock is held.\nA kind or inheritance change also deletes the superseded vertex of a\nnode that stays live under the same uuid; the retention predicate keeps\nthat node''s fields, which a new test pins.\n\nMeasured on a copy of a customer database (539k default-branch\nexistence edges, a branch forked 20 days earlier): the lookup takes\n0.22 s for 18,638 uuids, where reading them page by page takes 2.2 s.\n18,627 of them are vertices a kind migration superseded; the retention\nre-evaluation over all of them adds 1.2 s inside the rebase transaction\nand closes nothing. The stored base diff listed none of the 11 real\ndeletions.\n\nUpdate FR-007 and the research, plan and tasks records that chose the\nbase-branch diff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1502f3f830b6f8f64731f51f6e507da2a53a0b53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/1502f3f830b6f8f64731f51f6e507da2a53a0b53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKGM2NDA5MGY2M2NjNGFkNTFkNjA3MmVlZTlmZDBjMTU0MzVjNGViMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497","sha":"0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497"}],"sha":"c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/c64090f63cc4ad51d6072eee9fd0c15435c4eb0e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:15:10Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:55:13Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): scope the base-branch diff for a branch with no diffed changes\n\nThe base-branch run of the diff calculation is scoped to the fields the\nbranch changed. The node, field and property path queries turned an\nempty field-specifier map into None, because the map defines __len__,\nand two None lists select the unscoped entry clause meant for the\nbranch run. A branch whose diff is empty, such as one whose only\nchanges are git-sync bookkeeping on its repository, therefore got a\nbase diff holding every change made on the default branch since it was\ncreated: 383k nodes on a large dataset, including an IP namespace with\n204,878 relationship elements whose save exhausted database memory\nduring a rebase.\n\nTest the specifier maps for None instead of for truthiness.\n\nThe rebase depends on the old behaviour: it retires the branch-agnostic\nfields of default-branch deletions by reading the nodes the stored base\ndiff marks as removed, and that diff lists them only for a branch whose\ndiff is empty. Two tests in test_on_rebase.py fail with this change. On\nstable the same retirement already misses those deletions for any\nbranch with a diffed change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2482b065ddb080a4587be751c9a93c896a984271","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/2482b065ddb080a4587be751c9a93c896a984271"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDBhZWU3NTEzZTkyOWU4MTY3MmZmMDM5YTZjNzczZWNiNjg1YzA0OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/67c85f68331c6ddf849c3d64aa5f3b4ddf318979","sha":"67c85f68331c6ddf849c3d64aa5f3b4ddf318979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/67c85f68331c6ddf849c3d64aa5f3b4ddf318979"}],"sha":"0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/0aee7513e929e81672ff039a6c773ecb685c0497"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/67c85f68331c6ddf849c3d64aa5f3b4ddf318979/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:45:19Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:20:10Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"fix(diff): look up relationship elements by index when saving a diff\n\nThe save query upserted each relationship element with a MERGE on the\nDIFF_HAS_ELEMENT pattern, which walks every element already attached\nto the relationship group for each row. For a node related to many\nobjects, such as an IP namespace after a bulk IP address import, the\nsave was quadratic in the number of peers.\n\nAdd a RANGE index on DiffRelationshipElement(path_identifier, peer_id)\nand replace the MERGE with a seek on that pair, checking the\nDIFF_HAS_ELEMENT edge from the element side and creating the element\nwhen none is attached. A seek on peer_id alone would return every\nelement pointing at that peer across all stored diffs, so a peer\nshared by many nodes would turn quadratic instead. Server startup\ncreates missing indexes, so no migration is needed.\n\nMeasured with PROFILE on neo4j 2026.05 community, with 200k elements\nacross five stored diffs:\n- re-saving a node with 20,000 existing elements: 132 s / 801M db hits\n  -> 1.2 s / 1.9M db hits\n- saving a new node with 4,000 elements: 2.9 s / 32M -> 0.37 s / 332k\n- 1,000 nodes sharing one peer: unchanged (0.54 s -> 0.31 s re-save,\n  0.12 s -> 0.14 s new)\n\nThe same node in the base and the branch diff holds identical\n(path_identifier, peer_id) pairs, so a new test checks that re-saving\nkeeps one set of elements per diff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Alex Gittings <agitting96@gmail.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76f59c2c1aeeec1c5df2cdae9ce5158d6e9d9bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/76f59c2c1aeeec1c5df2cdae9ce5158d6e9d9bd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/67c85f68331c6ddf849c3d64aa5f3b4ddf318979","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":