ic"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/19c7d8bb5e3fb64b60dda3308cde01f8f5639345","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDE5YzdkOGJiNWUzZmI2NGI2MGRkYTMzMDhjZGUwMWY4ZjU2MzkzNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197","sha":"030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197"}],"sha":"19c7d8bb5e3fb64b60dda3308cde01f8f5639345","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/19c7d8bb5e3fb64b60dda3308cde01f8f5639345"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15846100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saltas888","id":15846100,"login":"saltas888","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODQ2MTAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saltas888","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:05:05Z","email":"d.saltaferis@gmail.com","name":"Saltaferis Dimitrios"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:05:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: fine tune context + harness (#10723)\n\n* docs(agents): load every AGENTS.md through a CLAUDE.md shim\n\nWith a root CLAUDE.md present, Claude Code reads no AGENTS.md below it on\nits own, so backend/, docs/ and development/grafana/ never reached a\nsession: only frontend/app/ had a CLAUDE.md importing its AGENTS.md.\n\nAdd the missing shims, each exactly `@AGENTS.md`, and trim\nfrontend/app/CLAUDE.md to the same line. Anything else in a CLAUDE.md is\ninvisible to harnesses that read only AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): inject a clock in time-dependent tests, not freezegun\n\nThe testing rule listed freezegun as an acceptable mocking exception,\nwhile the guideline it names as its full reference rules freezegun out,\nsince it is not a project dependency, and prescribes an injected clock.\nThe rule is what Claude Code loads, so sessions saw the wrong answer.\n\nDrop the bullet and state the guideline''s rule: time-dependent logic\ntakes a Callable[[], float] clock defaulting to time.monotonic, and the\ntest passes a fake it advances.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): move rule bodies into guidelines every harness reads\n\nOnly Claude Code loads .agents/rules, so a rule that holds guidance no doc\nrepeats is invisible to every other harness. Three rules did:\n\n- code-doc-style: its full text moves to dev/guidelines/code-doc-style.md.\n  The rule stays always loaded and keeps its four hard rules, one line\n  each.\n- python-module-layout: its explanation moves into a \"Module layout\"\n  section of dev/guidelines/backend/python.md. The imports half joins the\n  existing Imports section, now a subsection of it, rather than\n  repeating that section''s opening rule.\n- backend-component-design: its body moves to\n  dev/guidelines/backend/component-design.md. The rule, still injected on\n  every backend/infrahub/**/*.py read although its own scope excludes\n  single-function tweaks, shrinks to the scope paragraph and one line per\n  core rule, from about 15 KB to about 2 KB.\n\nEach rule ends with a pointer to its guideline. The dev/ docs and the\nharvesting-review skill that linked a rule file now link the guideline,\nand the root AGENTS.md lists both new guidelines with a load trigger.\nMoved text is verbatim, apart from the breadcrumb line and a relative\nlink the new location needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): name harness-loaded files once and link every doc\n\nA path to a file a harness loads on its own (an AGENTS.md, a rule, a\ncommand) loads it a second time when an agent follows it. Remove those\npointers:\n\n- Drop the root AGENTS.md link from the component AGENTS.md files and the\n  backend/docs AGENTS.md links from dev/ breadcrumbs and See Also lists;\n  every session already has the root one, and the component ones load\n  with the area.\n- Name /pre-ci and the commands in dev/README.md by slash name, and\n  describe _shared.md as the partial the flows read.\n- Say in typing.md which of its rules are the hard ones instead of\n  pointing at the rule file, and state migrate-feature-page''s lint\n  requirement without citing docs/AGENTS.md.\n- Mark the lines that name an AGENTS.md as the file a skill audits or\n  greps with the context-lint allow marker.\n\nLink the docs nothing named: the permission-checker guide from\nbackend/AGENTS.md, the date-rendering and object-file knowledge docs from\nfrontend/app/AGENTS.md, and the ADR template from dev/README.md. Delete\nthe legacy dev/skills/ folder, whose skills nothing loaded, and drop the\ndev/skills tree from the good-organization example. Name\ndevelopment/grafana/AGENTS.md in the root Component Maps, which is how\nCodex finds a nested AGENTS.md.\n\nCorrect dev/documentation-architecture.md: it described a\ndev/guidelines/frontend/README.md index that does not exist. The\ncomponent AGENTS.md is the index, and the doc now says how a component\nAGENTS.md reaches Claude Code (the CLAUDE.md beside it) and Codex (the\nroot AGENTS.md naming it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): scope the architecture doc''s rule claims and fix two digests\n\nThe architecture doc now says what Codex loads by default, limits the\none-line-per-rule claim to the consolidated rules, and its claim that every\nrule''s guideline is linked from an AGENTS.md holds now that the root\nAGENTS.md names the backend testing guideline. The code-doc-style digest\nkeeps the version-constraint qualifier, and typing.md lists two hard rules\nplus the isinstance preference, matching its own sections.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): describe AggregatedConstraintChecker''s dispatch accurately\n\nThe component-design guidance called it the canonical first-match example,\nbut it runs every checker that supports the request and aggregates their\nresults. This sentence came over verbatim from the rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): name the AGENTS.md files as a group in two skills\n\naudit-docs and harvesting-review named backend/ and frontend/app/ AGENTS.md\nby path behind allow markers. They now name the component AGENTS.md files as\na group, and the harvesting grep covers all five instead of three.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): load the coding guidelines for reviews too\n\nA review needs the same guidelines as writing the code, so their load\nconditions in AGENTS.md and backend/AGENTS.md now cover reviewing. The\nAlways Do line said \"diagnosing\", which was vague; it now names tracking\ndown a bug, reviewing a change or modifying code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): give each typing trigger its own \"when\" in backend/AGENTS.md\n\n\"narrowing a union or an optional or reviewing code that does\" stacked\nthree \"or\"s, so \"reviewing\" could read as one more thing to narrow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbd3a87d589f54ae283f88657a3ad09309c95664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/cbd3a87d589f54ae283f88657a3ad09309c95664"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197","verification":{"payload":"tree cbd3a87d589f54ae283f88657a3ad09309c95664\nparent 7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c\nauthor Saltaferis Dimitrios <d.saltaferis@gmail.com> 1790593505 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790593505 +0200\n\ndocs: fine tune context + harness (#10723)\n\n* docs(agents): load every AGENTS.md through a CLAUDE.md shim\n\nWith a root CLAUDE.md present, Claude Code reads no AGENTS.md below it on\nits own, so backend/, docs/ and development/grafana/ never reached a\nsession: only frontend/app/ had a CLAUDE.md importing its AGENTS.md.\n\nAdd the missing shims, each exactly `@AGENTS.md`, and trim\nfrontend/app/CLAUDE.md to the same line. Anything else in a CLAUDE.md is\ninvisible to harnesses that read only AGENTS.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): inject a clock in time-dependent tests, not freezegun\n\nThe testing rule listed freezegun as an acceptable mocking exception,\nwhile the guideline it names as its full reference rules freezegun out,\nsince it is not a project dependency, and prescribes an injected clock.\nThe rule is what Claude Code loads, so sessions saw the wrong answer.\n\nDrop the bullet and state the guideline''s rule: time-dependent logic\ntakes a Callable[[], float] clock defaulting to time.monotonic, and the\ntest passes a fake it advances.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): move rule bodies into guidelines every harness reads\n\nOnly Claude Code loads .agents/rules, so a rule that holds guidance no doc\nrepeats is invisible to every other harness. Three rules did:\n\n- code-doc-style: its full text moves to dev/guidelines/code-doc-style.md.\n  The rule stays always loaded and keeps its four hard rules, one line\n  each.\n- python-module-layout: its explanation moves into a \"Module layout\"\n  section of dev/guidelines/backend/python.md. The imports half joins the\n  existing Imports section, now a subsection of it, rather than\n  repeating that section''s opening rule.\n- backend-component-design: its body moves to\n  dev/guidelines/backend/component-design.md. The rule, still injected on\n  every backend/infrahub/**/*.py read although its own scope excludes\n  single-function tweaks, shrinks to the scope paragraph and one line per\n  core rule, from about 15 KB to about 2 KB.\n\nEach rule ends with a pointer to its guideline. The dev/ docs and the\nharvesting-review skill that linked a rule file now link the guideline,\nand the root AGENTS.md lists both new guidelines with a load trigger.\nMoved text is verbatim, apart from the breadcrumb line and a relative\nlink the new location needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): name harness-loaded files once and link every doc\n\nA path to a file a harness loads on its own (an AGENTS.md, a rule, a\ncommand) loads it a second time when an agent follows it. Remove those\npointers:\n\n- Drop the root AGENTS.md link from the component AGENTS.md files and the\n  backend/docs AGENTS.md links from dev/ breadcrumbs and See Also lists;\n  every session already has the root one, and the component ones load\n  with the area.\n- Name /pre-ci and the commands in dev/README.md by slash name, and\n  describe _shared.md as the partial the flows read.\n- Say in typing.md which of its rules are the hard ones instead of\n  pointing at the rule file, and state migrate-feature-page''s lint\n  requirement without citing docs/AGENTS.md.\n- Mark the lines that name an AGENTS.md as the file a skill audits or\n  greps with the context-lint allow marker.\n\nLink the docs nothing named: the permission-checker guide from\nbackend/AGENTS.md, the date-rendering and object-file knowledge docs from\nfrontend/app/AGENTS.md, and the ADR template from dev/README.md. Delete\nthe legacy dev/skills/ folder, whose skills nothing loaded, and drop the\ndev/skills tree from the good-organization example. Name\ndevelopment/grafana/AGENTS.md in the root Component Maps, which is how\nCodex finds a nested AGENTS.md.\n\nCorrect dev/documentation-architecture.md: it described a\ndev/guidelines/frontend/README.md index that does not exist. The\ncomponent AGENTS.md is the index, and the doc now says how a component\nAGENTS.md reaches Claude Code (the CLAUDE.md beside it) and Codex (the\nroot AGENTS.md naming it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): scope the architecture doc''s rule claims and fix two digests\n\nThe architecture doc now says what Codex loads by default, limits the\none-line-per-rule claim to the consolidated rules, and its claim that every\nrule''s guideline is linked from an AGENTS.md holds now that the root\nAGENTS.md names the backend testing guideline. The code-doc-style digest\nkeeps the version-constraint qualifier, and typing.md lists two hard rules\nplus the isinstance preference, matching its own sections.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): describe AggregatedConstraintChecker''s dispatch accurately\n\nThe component-design guidance called it the canonical first-match example,\nbut it runs every checker that supports the request and aggregates their\nresults. This sentence came over verbatim from the rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): name the AGENTS.md files as a group in two skills\n\naudit-docs and harvesting-review named backend/ and frontend/app/ AGENTS.md\nby path behind allow markers. They now name the component AGENTS.md files as\na group, and the harvesting grep covers all five instead of three.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): load the coding guidelines for reviews too\n\nA review needs the same guidelines as writing the code, so their load\nconditions in AGENTS.md and backend/AGENTS.md now cover reviewing. The\nAlways Do line said \"diagnosing\", which was vague; it now names tracking\ndown a bug, reviewing a change or modifying code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): give each typing trigger its own \"when\" in backend/AGENTS.md\n\n\"narrowing a union or an optional or reviewing code that does\" stacked\nthree \"or\"s, so \"reviewing\" could read as one more thing to narrow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquknhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA68sQAIhLTOt/Ty7Mh7/1LcSaSiea\nWN9Pi2BUPG5l1w90mO1m77u38oYqv7jIUNB0NP5vwQ09lOFt0soaSWKZf+cIOaL4\nhF+Hj3+b7BYaM/kPpespc3uPXKhWkOluNzTr2ecsQ1kIvKZK7bFjEudCfg0cD6FI\nNLOcnWAdMDfdre1D/htBpXhPRyBnl08PqVxyb0PkiOPZPR7YmEevSAGWS9ydWMDF\nVmZuOcTw3lq3bSqY1sMqySeLoJ1qgzZTFuUq70P7WJMM87rJ211fSQmKCse2lPPB\nNMAHx4Srngd7FhKhQfVGWHyNJESff+j4rW2DWS/1xgIhu8Fh/CKAv8LRfAXEs9HY\nJeP9Jz+1U+r1Fx5GPoV2o7obF3UnpczmUiUx7NQ0le+UUBgCI9ZBytYLpKM7N6w1\n8wzLxI4IHOBzkXARdJckZ/F4tnpi6tYdkzMzWms5+56yzTDrNs2xKUBh0Zo3SbXB\nPsRDkzEmW/bRoHFlm2ALg9+TTd2qV+H1cwQaPvRXjcJV2J+ItUQ3sj1aJLzCcLy1\nTmDmMiujKIigrihfgFOMaOPPRU4SxG3VOIkATU5++oZogeH0BOEfnKuDx6ttjfeM\nv5yM8crr0/G8C3Fs7XUGteLYiluIVKAEQ8NJ2uUe2Ss7t2wpb4TTeLmWI5iNBMYl\nRLg+XEQ+MPDWvkBbJ7vZ\n=541l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T11:05:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDAzMGIyNWJkYjQyYmE3NjUwN2VjY2QyNWVjMzE5NWZmNjAyMWMxOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c","sha":"7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c"}],"sha":"030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/030b25bdb42ba76507eccd25ec3195ff6021c197"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/commits/7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:02:27Z","email":"infrahub@opsmill.com","name":"Infrahub"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:32:08Z","email":"fatih-acar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"fatih-acar"},"message":"docs(deploy): add Helm persistence values for every bundled component\n\nThe storage persistence warning on the Community and Enterprise install\npages named only Neo4j, although the bundled task manager PostgreSQL\ndatabase also runs on emptyDir by default and loses its task history and\nworkflow state when its pod is rescheduled. Recommend persistence on\nNeo4j and PostgreSQL at minimum, and add a values example that also\ncovers Redis and RabbitMQ. The production values example now persists\nPostgreSQL too.\n\nRendering the Infrahub 4.33.3 and Infrahub Enterprise 4.19.3 charts with\nhelm template confirms each example produces volume claims on the\nexpected StatefulSets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac84354733b6cf85a365e0e1af4f76589a8a3571","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/trees/ac84354733b6cf85a365e0e1af4f76589a8a3571"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opsmill/infrahub/git/commits/7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fatih-acar","id":15028881,"login":"fatih-acar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatih-acar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opsmill/infrahub/commit/7c101af1d825496b61fe685a8e0e30e851f7cf5c","node_id":"C_kwDOH4TYMtoAKDdjMTAxYWYxZDgyNTQ5NmI2MWZlNjg1YThlMGUzMGU4NTFmN2NmNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com